                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#members> (cdao:BFO_0000142
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000146
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000147).
_:B1b3d9a6979aa269893b442d32a89253b cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/107-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000011;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (r) (if (SpatioTemporalRegion r) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion r r))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [107-002] ".
_:B1b96dea22e3880a9c4627b9dc102049b cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/037-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000018;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A zero-dimensional spatial region is a point in space. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [037-001])"@en.
_:B1c1bdc3d5caa5fa797fe8f0f9a597482 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/107-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000601;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000011;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "Every spatiotemporal region s is such that s occupies_spatiotemporal_region s. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [107-002])"@en.
_:B1db3131599243ffee8d81159ee21a45f cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/138-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000182;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A history is a process that is the sum of the totality of processes taking place in the spatiotemporal region occupied by a material entity or site, including processes on the surface of the entity or within the cavities to which it serves as host. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [138-001])"@en.
_:B201c4c3dfa38a13eabfd4d89536fe3e2 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#members> (cdao:BFO_0000004
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000020
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000031).
_:B20e77d7c7c749eedb8ccf74cfc42cb9f cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/0000301>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000116;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000027;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "An entity a is an object aggregate if and only if there is a mutually exhaustive and pairwise disjoint partition of a into objects ".
_:B21a4b4daef281294377f9b0640269805 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/061-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000023;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x) (if (Role x) (RealizableEntity x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [061-001] ".
_:B24c0d2fb092362da2b1727b3a9401440 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/094-005>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000144;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "b process_profile_of c holds when b proper_occurrent_part_of c& there is some proper_occurrent_part d of c which has no parts in common with b & is mutually dependent on b& is such that b, c and d occupy the same temporal region (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [094-005])"@en.
_:B26534ebca1f090d563ceecd1518e93c6 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/126-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000002;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x y) (if (and (Continuant x) (exists (t) (hasContinuantPartOfAt y x t))) (Continuant y))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [126-001] ".
_:B26fac8d163d06888ed1229d323516e86 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/074-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000115;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000031;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "b is a generically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant that g-depends_on one or more other entities. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [074-001])"@en.
_:B294863567e41152149a5ba3410b15d0f cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/018-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000601;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000004;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "For every independent continuant b and time t during the region of time spanned by its life, there are entities which s-depends_on b during t. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [018-002])"@en.
_:B2a6a2ec391b3847c83410e64e8864f97 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/058-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000017;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "To say that b is a realizable entity is to say that b is a specifically dependent continuant that inheres in some independent continuant which is not a spatial region and is of a type instances of which are realized in processes of a correlated type. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [058-002])"@en.
_:B2ae8530f9fab079116620b3672a1c380 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/101-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000008;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x y) (if (and (TemporalRegion x) (occurrentPartOf y x)) (TemporalRegion y))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [101-001] ".
_:B2bddc4919fabff7bb6874088174f6f58 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/105-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000019;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x) (if (exists (t) (and (existsAt x t) (Quality x))) (forall (t_1) (if (existsAt x t_1) (Quality x))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [105-001] ".
_:B2f5813d84e9ae731753eea832656c755 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/038-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000026;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A one-dimensional spatial region is a line or aggregate of lines stretching from one point in space to another. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [038-001])"@en.
_:B3049e63f881fe3f2dae2893bc5a81d47 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/074-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000031;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(iff (GenericallyDependentContinuant a) (and (Continuant a) (exists (b t) (genericallyDependsOnAt a b t)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [074-001] ".
_:B36790cce23b5e87c092bcbe58404c5b7 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/050-003>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000115;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000020;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "b is a specifically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant & there is some independent continuant c which is not a spatial region and which is such that b s-depends_on c at every time t during the course of b’s existence. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [050-003])"@en.
_:B36c02e283a236da4af41187d37cd4990 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/099-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000011;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x t) (if (SpatioTemporalRegion x) (exists (y) (and (SpatialRegion y) (spatiallyProjectsOntoAt x y t))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [099-001] ".
_:B386833d22af4f53d7cbf79587212d28f cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/035-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000006;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A spatial region is a continuant entity that is a continuant_part_of spaceR as defined relative to some frame R. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [035-001])"@en.
_:B3de3cd5622af9c1de9cb5ead1271eb6a cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/103-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000038;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A one-dimensional temporal region is a temporal region that is extended. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [103-001])"@en.
_:B3fd90c2e73a45b10cc9c8650951e80c1 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/083-003>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000015;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(iff (Process a) (and (Occurrent a) (exists (b) (properTemporalPartOf b a)) (exists (c t) (and (MaterialEntity c) (specificallyDependsOnAt a c t))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [083-003] ".
_:B40fe38812ebada4744accc728762b228 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/058-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000017;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x) (if (RealizableEntity x) (and (SpecificallyDependentContinuant x) (exists (y) (and (IndependentContinuant y) (not (SpatialRegion y)) (inheresIn x y)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [058-002] ".
_:B4141e7d25b71c25ff8844995de01d49d cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/093-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000144;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(iff (ProcessProfile a) (exists (b) (and (Process b) (processProfileOf a b)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [093-002] ".
_:B41ebb5d2e87a001d89fca3ffc39aab5d cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/0000008>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000116;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000140;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "Continuant fiat boundary doesn't have a closure axiom because the subclasses don't necessarily exhaust all possibilites. An example would be the mereological sum of two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary and a one dimensional continuant fiat boundary that doesn't overlap it. The situation is analogous to temporal and spatial regions."@en.
_:B43b8a859052ae94b76bd71accfaf7791 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/020-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000601;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000040;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "Every entity which has a material entity as continuant part is a material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [020-002])"@en.
_:B456f200a8dbd6fc6c3491d3046f2e443 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/060-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000017;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x t) (if (RealizableEntity x) (exists (y) (and (IndependentContinuant y) (not (SpatialRegion y)) (bearerOfAt y x t))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [060-002] ".
_:B469cee5f123c22db40d75a8e79199441 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/064-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000034;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A function is a disposition that exists in virtue of the bearer’s physical make-up and this physical make-up is something the bearer possesses because it came into being, either through evolution (in the case of natural biological entities) or through intentional design (in the case of artifacts), in order to realize processes of a certain sort. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [064-001])"@en.
_:B4bdab2d27b917c88cb0377e80a4eb7a2 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/031-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000147;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(iff (ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [031-001] ".
_:B4bdb1aa85ae4c98140b158c165fac4d7 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#members> (cdao:BFO_0000009
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000018
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000026
                                                                             cdao:BFO_0000028).
_:B4d03177c6b125207fdfff72444d3b559 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/009-002>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000002;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x y) (if (and (Continuant x) (exists (t) (continuantPartOfAt y x t))) (Continuant y))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [009-002] ".
_:B4e2ce14515442a3b8386cd878fd6515e cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/064-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000034;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x) (if (Function x) (Disposition x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [064-001] ".
_:B4ff9c89aec4792b752c4ecc3c1e554eb cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/040-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000600;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000028;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "A three-dimensional spatial region is a spatial region that is of three dimensions. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [040-001])"@en.
_:B50f9b3eec390b6ac68a68183372ae3d1 cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/0000005>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    rdfs:comment "per discussion with Barry Smith";
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000116;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000020;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "Specifically dependent continuant doesn't have a closure axiom because the subclasses don't necessarily exhaust all possibilites. We're not sure what else will develop here, but for example there are questions such as what are promises, obligation, etc."@en.
_:B51b35671ae4e875d2c0c36e7464906f7 cdao:IAO_0000116 "consider if we really want to be so strict here . . . ie maybe we we say that they have not been output from an 'establishing cell line' process, but in some cases a passage or two may be allowed for a primary culture.  the establishing of a line requires some  procedss that attains a degree of homogeneity in the culture.";
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> rdfs:subClassOf;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:OBI_0100061;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> cdao:OBI_0600037 ; 
                                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000312 ; 
                                                                                     a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
_:B55af5243cc9aa6527d767074c200124a cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/126-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000601;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000002;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "if b is a continuant and if, for some t, c has_continuant_part b at t, then c is a continuant. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [126-001])"@en.
_:B561cc6554d7b0be81f25a1f900e3616d cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/050-003>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000020;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(iff (SpecificallyDependentContinuant a) (and (Continuant a) (forall (t) (if (existsAt a t) (exists (b) (and (IndependentContinuant b) (not (SpatialRegion b)) (specificallyDependsOnAt a b t))))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [050-003] ".
_:B56efee1696a0538f9ad210094a0dd10e cdao:IAO_0010000 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/040-001>;
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> cdao:IAO_0000602;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:BFO_0000028;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> "(forall (x) (if (ThreeDimensionalSpatialRegion x) (SpatialRegion x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [040-001] ".
_:B59392c614cc4a105655987f82774b97c cdao:IAO_0000116 "'derives from' is transitive, so even cell line cells created through modification of an existing cell line cell have derived_from some initial primary cultured cell that existed at some point in time.";
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom>;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> rdfs:subClassOf;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> cdao:CLO_0000001;
