cdao:IAO_0000001 cdao:IAO_0000111 "conditional specification"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a directive information entity that specifies what should happen if the trigger condition is fulfilled"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000349"@en,
                                  "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "conditional specification"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000033.
cdao:IAO_0000002 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "example to be eventually removed"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000003 cdao:IAO_0000111 "measurement unit label"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Examples of measurement unit labels are liters, inches, weight per volume."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A measurement unit label is as a label that is part of a scalar measurement datum and denotes a unit of measure."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009-03-16: review of this term done during during the OBI workshop winter 2009 and the current definition was considered acceptable for use in OBI. If there is a need to modify this definition please notify OBI."@en,
                                  """2009-03-16: provenance: a term measurement unit was
proposed for OBI (OBI_0000176) , edited by Chris Stoeckert and
Cristian Cocos, and subsequently moved to IAO where the objective for
which the original term was defined was satisfied with the definition
of this, different, term."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "measurement unit label"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000009.
cdao:IAO_0000004 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:IAO_0000032;
                 rdfs:label "has measurement value"@en;
                 rdfs:range xsd:double;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty>.
cdao:IAO_0000005 cdao:IAO_0000111 "objective specification"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "In the protocol of a ChIP assay the objective specification says to identify protein and DNA interaction."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a directive information entity that describes an intended process endpoint. When part of a plan specification the concretization is realized in a planned process in which the bearer tries to effect the world so that the process endpoint is achieved."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2014-03-31: In the example of usage (\"In the protocol of a ChIP assay the objective specification says to identify protein and DNA interaction\") there is a protocol which is the ChIP assay protocol. In addition to being concretized on paper, the protocol can be concretized as a realizable entity, such as a plan that inheres in a person. The objective specification is the part that says that some protein and DNA interactions are identified. This is a specification of a process endpoint: the boundary in the process before which they are not identified and after which they are. During the realization of the plan, the goal is to get to the point of having the interactions, and participants in the realization of the plan try to do that."""@en,
                                  "Answers the question, why did you do this experiment?"@en,
                                  """2009-03-16: original definition when imported from OBI read: \"objective is an non realizable information entity which can serve as that  proper part of a plan towards which the realization of the plan is directed.\""""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Barry Smith"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "goal specification"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI Plan and Planned Process/Roles Branch"@en,
                                  "OBI_0000217"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "objective specification"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000033.
cdao:IAO_0000006 cdao:IAO_0000111 "narrative object"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Examples of narrative objects are reports, journal  articles, and patents submission."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A narrative object is an information content entity that is a set of propositions."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "agree - DENRIE. Issue(alan) do we only mean text? What about a story told by mime. Does music count? (no) what about an oral report. Regarding definition, saying it is a set of propositions means we loose the idea that wording matters. Maybe adjust saying a narrative object has some relationshop to a set of propositions"@en,
                                  "2009-08-10 Alan Ruttenberg: Larry Hunter suggests that this be obsoleted and replaced by 'textual entity' and 'figure'. Alan restored as there are OBI dependencies and this merits further discussion"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000013"@en,
                                  "group:OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "narrative object"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:IAO_0000007 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Pour the contents of flask 1 into flask 2"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a directive information entity that describes an action the bearer will take"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI Plan and Planned Process branch"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "action specification"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000033.
cdao:IAO_0000008 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_artifact";
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000009 cdao:IAO_0000111 "datum label"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A label is a symbol that is part of some other datum and is used to either partially define  the denotation of that datum or to provide a means for identifying the datum as a member of the set of data with the same label"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "http://www.golovchenko.org/cgi-bin/wnsearch?q=label#4n"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: IAO"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 """9/22/11 BP: changed the rdfs:label for this class from 'label' to 'datum label' to convey that this class is not intended to cover all kinds of labels (stickers, radiolabels, etc.), and not even all kind of textual labels, but rather the kind of labels occuring in a datum. 
""";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "datum label"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:IAO_0000010 cdao:IAO_0000111 "software"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """Software is a plan specification composed of a series of instructions that can be 
interpreted by or directly executed by a processing unit."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "see sourceforge tracker discussion at http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?func=detail&aid=1958818&group_id=177891&atid=886178"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "software"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000104.
cdao:IAO_0000012 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolete_digital entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A digital entity is an information entity which is a collection of bits that can be interpreted by a computer. Two digital entities are the same if they are bitwise identical."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """3/22/2009 Alan Ruttenberg, obsoleted per http://groups.google.com/group/information-ontology/browse_thread/thread/789ad4b7708d5cf4

Superclass was 'digitial quality'"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000261",
                                  "group:OBI"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete2_digital entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000013 cdao:IAO_0000111 "journal article"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Examples are articles published in the journals, Nature and Science. The content can often be cited by reference to a paper based encoding, e.g.  Authors, Title of article, Journal name, date or year of publication, volume and page number."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a report that is published in a journal"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000159"@en,
                                  "group:OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "journal article"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000088.
cdao:IAO_0000015 cdao:IAO_0000111 "information carrier"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "In the case of a printed paperback novel the physicality of the ink and of the paper form part of the information bearer. The qualities of appearing black and having a certain pattern for the ink and appearing white for the paper form part of the information carrier in this case."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A quality of an information bearer that imparts the information content"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2014-03-10: We are not certain that all information carriers are qualities. There was a discussion of dropping it.",
                                  "12/15/09: There is a concern that some ways that carry information may be processes rather than qualities, such as in a 'delayed wave carrier'."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Smith, Ceusters, Ruttenberg, 2000 years of philosophy"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "information carrier"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000019;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:BFO_0000019
                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000030 ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:IAO_0000017 cdao:IAO_0000111 "model number"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A model number is an information content entity specifically borne by catalogs, design specifications, advertising materials, inventory systems and similar  that is about manufactured objects of the same class. The model number is an alternative term for the class. The manufactered objects may or may not also bear the model number. Model numbers can be encoded in a variety of other information objects, such as bar codes, numerals, or patterns of dots."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "manufactered items may have more than one model number, sometimes by rebranding, or because companies are sold and the products issued new model numbers"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "model number"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000028.
cdao:IAO_0000018 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000226;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_material_entity";
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000019 cdao:IAO_0000111 "binary digital entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "MS Word document, ZIP file, DICOM file, JPEG file"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A binary digital entity is a digital entity that is encoded in a way that is not easily human readable and that contains other than text characters."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "digital_entity"@en,
                                  """3/22/2009 Alan Ruttenberg, obsoleted per http://groups.google.com/group/information-ontology/browse_thread/thread/789ad4b7708d5cf4
Superclass was 'digital entity'"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000244",
                                  "group:OBI"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete2_binary digital entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000024 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The length of a ruler.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a unit of measure is the quality of some material entity compared to which another quality is some multiple of.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Smith, Ceusters, Ruttenberg, 2000 years of philosophy";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_unit of measure";
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000025 cdao:IAO_0000111 "programming language"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "R, Perl, Java"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A language in which source code is written that is intended to be executed/run by a software interpreter. Programming languages are ways to write instructions that specify what to do, and sometimes, how to do it."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:OBI"@en,
                                  "OBI_0000058"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "programming language"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000104.
cdao:IAO_0000027 cdao:IAO_0000111 "data item"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Data items include counts of things, analyte concentrations, and statistical summaries."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a data item is an information content entity that is intended to be a truthful statement about something (modulo, e.g., measurement precision or other systematic errors) and is constructed/acquired by a method which reliably tends to produce (approximately) truthful statements."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009-03-16: removed datum as alternative term as datum specifically refers to singular form, and is thus not an exact synonym."@en,
                                  "2009-03-16: data item deliberatly ambiguous: we merged data set and datum to be one entity, not knowing how to define singular versus plural. So data item is more general than datum."@en,
                                  "2/2/2009 Alan and Bjoern discussing FACS run output data. This is a data item because it is about the cell population. Each element records an event and is typically further composed a set of measurment data items that record the fluorescent intensity stimulated by one of the lasers."@en,
                                  """JAR: datum     -- well, this will be very tricky to define, but maybe some 
information-like stuff that might be put into a computer and that is 
meant, by someone, to denote and/or to be interpreted by some 
process... I would include lists, tables, sentences... I think I might 
defer to Barry, or to Brian Cantwell Smith

JAR: A data item is an approximately justified approximately true approximate belief"""@en,
                                  "2014-03-31: See discussion at http://odontomachus.wordpress.com/2014/03/30/aboutness-objects-propositions/";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jonathan Rees"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "data"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "data item"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:IAO_0000028 cdao:IAO_0000111 "symbol"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """a written proper name such as \"OBI\""""@en,
                                  """a serial number such as \"12324X\""""@en,
                                  "a stop sign"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An information content entity that is a mark(s) or character(s) used as a conventional representation of another entity."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2014-03-31: We would like to have a deeper analysis of 'mark' and 'sign' in the future (see https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/154)."@en,
                                  "20091104, MC: this needs work and will most probably change"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jonathan Rees"@en,
                                  "PERSON: James A. Overton"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "based on Oxford English Dictionary"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "symbol"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:IAO_0000029 cdao:IAO_0000111 "numeral"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A symbol that denotes a number."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jonathan Rees"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "numeral"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000028.
cdao:IAO_0000030 cdao:IAO_0000111 "information content entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Examples of information content entites include journal articles, data, graphical layouts, and graphs."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2014-03-10: The use of \"thing\" is intended to be general enough to include universals and configurations (see https://groups.google.com/d/msg/information-ontology/GBxvYZCk1oc/-L6B5fSBBTQJ)."""@en,
                                  """information_content_entity 'is_encoded_in' some digital_entity in obi before split (040907). information_content_entity 'is_encoded_in' some physical_document in obi before split (040907).

Previous. An information content entity is a non-realizable information entity that 'is encoded in' some digital or physical entity."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000142"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "information content entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000001 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:IAO_0000136 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:BFO_0000031.
cdao:IAO_0000031 cdao:IAO_0000111 "integer numeral"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a numeral that denotes an integer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jonathan Rees"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "integer numeral"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000029.
cdao:IAO_0000032 cdao:IAO_0000112 "10 feet. 3 ml."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a scalar measurement datum is a measurement datum that is composed of two parts, numerals and a unit label."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Would write this as: has_part some 'measurement unit label' and has_part some numeral and has_part exactly 2, except for the fact that this won't let us take advantage of OWL reasoning over the numbers. Instead use has measurment value property to represent the same. Use has measurement unit label (subproperty of has_part) so we can easily say that there is only one of them."@en,
                                  """2009-03-16: we decided to keep datum singular in scalar measurement datum, as in
this case we explicitly refer to the singular form"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "scalar measurement datum"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000109,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#minCardinality> "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:IAO_0000039 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0001931 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0001938 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#minCardinality> "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:IAO_0000004 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:IAO_0000033 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An information content entity whose concretizations indicate to their bearer how to realize them in a process."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2009-03-16: provenance: a term realizable information entity was proposed for OBI (OBI_0000337) , edited by the PlanAndPlannedProcess branch. Original definition was  \"is the specification of a process that can be concretized and realized by an actor\" with alternative term  \"instruction\".It has been subsequently moved to IAO where the objective for which the original term was defined was satisfied with the definitionof this, different, term."""@en,
                                  "Werner pushed back on calling it realizable information entity as it isn't realizable. However this name isn't right either. An example would be a recipe. The realizable entity would be a plan, but the information entity isn't about the plan, it, once concretized, *is* the plan. -Alan"@en,
                                  "2013-05-30 Alan Ruttenberg: What differentiates a directive information entity from an information concretization is that it can have concretizations that are either qualities or realizable entities. The concretizations that are realizable entities are created when an individual chooses to take up the direction, i.e. has the intention to (try to) realize it."@en,
                                  """8/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: Changed label from \"information entity about a realizable\" after discussions at ICBO"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "directive information entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000017 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:IAO_0000136 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:IAO_0000034 cdao:IAO_0000111 "time trigger"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000124;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "revisit?"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000331"@en,
                                  "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "time trigger"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000001.
cdao:IAO_0000035 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolete_study interpretation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A study interpretation is a textual entity about the implications of a study result. Examples include discussion of whether a hypothesis is false, whether the study failed to address the hypothesis, and whether the study results have led to new hypotheses"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009-03-16: work has been done on this term during during the OBI workshop winter 2009 and the current definition was considered acceptable for use in OBI. If there is a need to modify this definition please notify OBI.",
                                  """The obsoleting of narrative object required a modest change in the definition of this term.  Circularity with \"interpretation... interprets\" has been removed, using \"about the implications\" instead."""@en,
                                  """2009-03-16: definition was \"A conclusion is a narrative object which can be published in a paper summerizing and interpreting a protocol application.\"""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Lawrence Hunter"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg",
                                  "PERSON: Melanie Courtot",
                                  "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "conclusion";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000005";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_study interpretation"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000037 cdao:IAO_0000111 "dot plot"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Dot plot of SSC-H and FSC-H."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000002;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A dot plot is a report graph which is a graphical representation of data where each data point is represented by a single dot placed on coordinates corresponding to data point values in particular dimensions."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "person:Allyson Lister"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:OBI"@en,
                                  "OBI_0000123"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "dot plot"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000038 cdao:IAO_0000111 "graph"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A diagram that presents one or more tuples of information by mapping those tuples in to a two dimensional space in a non arbitrary way."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Allyson Lister"@en,
                                  "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:OBI"@en,
                                  "OBI_0000240"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "graph"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000309.
cdao:IAO_0000039 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "has measurement unit label"@en;
                 rdfs:range cdao:IAO_0000003;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:BFO_0000051.
cdao:IAO_0000047 cdao:IAO_0000111 "text based digital entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "XML file, C++ source code file"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A text based digital entity is a digital entity that is encoded so that it only contains text characters."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """3/22/2009 Alan Ruttenberg, obsoleted per http://groups.google.com/group/information-ontology/browse_thread/thread/789ad4b7708d5cf4
superclass was 'digital document'"""@en,
                                  "digital_entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI_0000132",
                                  "group:OBI";
