cdao:IAO_0000115 cdao:IAO_0000111 "definition",
                                  "definition"@en,
                                  "textual definition";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The official OBI definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property. Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions."@en,
                                  "The official definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property. Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2012-04-05: 
Barry Smith

The official OBI definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property: 'Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions'  is terrible.

Can you fix to something like:

A statement of necessary and sufficient conditions explaining the meaning of an expression referring to a class or property.

Alan Ruttenberg

Your proposed definition is a reasonable candidate, except that it is very common that necessary and sufficient conditions are not given. Mostly they are necessary, occasionally they are necessary and sufficient or just sufficient. Often they use terms that are not themselves defined and so they effectively can't be evaluated by those criteria. 

On the specifics of the proposed definition:

We don't have definitions of 'meaning' or 'expression' or 'property'. For 'reference' in the intended sense I think we use the term 'denotation'. For 'expression', I think we you mean symbol, or identifier. For 'meaning' it differs for class and property. For class we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine whether an entity is instance of the class, or not. For property we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine, given a pair of potential relata, whether the assertion that the relation holds is true. The 'intended reader' part suggests that we also specify who, we expect, would be able to understand the definition, and also generalizes over human and computer reader to include textual and logical definition. 

Personally, I am more comfortable weakening definition to documentation, with instructions as to what is desirable. 

We also have the outstanding issue of how to aim different definitions to different audiences. A clinical audience reading chebi wants a different sort of definition documentation/definition from a chemistry trained audience, and similarly there is a need for a definition that is adequate for an ontologist to work with.  """@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "textual definition",
                            "definition",
                            "definition"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000116 cdao:IAO_0000111 "editor note"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An administrative note intended for its editor. It may not be included in the publication version of the ontology, so it should contain nothing necessary for end users to understand the ontology."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obfoundry.org/obo/obi>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "editor note"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000117 cdao:IAO_0000111 "term editor"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Name of editor entering the term in the file. The term editor is a point of contact for information regarding the term. The term editor may be, but is not always, the author of the definition, which may have been worked upon by several people"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "20110707, MC: label update to term editor and definition modified accordingly. See https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/115."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "term editor"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000118 cdao:IAO_0000111 "alternative term"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An alternative name for a class or property which means the same thing as the preferred name (semantically equivalent)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "alternative term"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000119 cdao:IAO_0000111 "definition source"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "formal citation, e.g. identifier in external database to indicate / attribute source(s) for the definition. Free text indicate / attribute source(s) for the definition. EXAMPLE: Author Name, URI, MeSH Term C04, PUBMED ID, Wiki uri on 31.01.2007"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en,
                                  "Discussion on obo-discuss mailing-list, see http://bit.ly/hgm99w";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "definition source"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000120 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Class has all its metadata, but is either not guaranteed to be in its final location in the asserted IS_A hierarchy or refers to another class that is not complete."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "metadata complete"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000121 cdao:IAO_0000115 "term created to ease viewing/sort terms for development purpose, and will not be included in a release"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg";
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "organizational term"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000122 cdao:IAO_0000115 """Class has undergone final review, is ready for use, and will be included in the next release. Any class lacking \"ready_for_release\" should be considered likely to change place in hierarchy, have its definition refined, or be obsoleted in the next release.  Those classes deemed \"ready_for_release\" will also derived from a chain of ancestor classes that are also \"ready_for_release.\""""@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "ready for release"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000123 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Class is being worked on; however, the metadata (including definition) are not complete or sufficiently clear to the branch editors."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "metadata incomplete"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000124 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Nothing done yet beyond assigning a unique class ID and proposing a preferred term."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "uncurated"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000125 cdao:IAO_0000115 "All definitions, placement in the asserted IS_A hierarchy and required minimal metadata are complete. The class is awaiting a final review by someone other than the term editor."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000078,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "pending final vetting"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000128 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000121;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """_identifier is a container under information content entity for collecting types of terms to indicate a specific instance or clas of what was used or participated in an investigation. Identifiers are borne by a product or its packaging, and can be encoded in a variety of other information objects, such as bar codes, numerals, or patterns of dots.

Note: everybody agreed that identifier is probably a too general term. We however felt that it would be appropriate to group \"identifiying\" terms under some kind of umbrella. We therefore propose to use _identifier for that purpose. As per OBI conventions, the _ prefixing identifier indicates that this is a helper class and shouldn't be considered as final.""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000226;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_identifier";
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000129 cdao:IAO_0000111 "version number"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A version number is an information content entity which is a sequence of characters borne by part of each of a class of manufactured products or its packaging and indicates its order within a set of other products having the same name."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Note: we feel that at the moment we are happy with a general version number, and that we will subclass as needed in the future. For example, see 7. genome sequence version"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: IAO"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "version number"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000028.
cdao:IAO_0000131 cdao:IAO_0000111 "serial number"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A serial number is an information content entity which is a unique sequence of characters borne by part of manufactured product or its packaging that is assigned to each individual in some class of products, and so can serve as a way to identify an individual product within the class. Serial numbers can be encoded in a variety of other information objects, such as bar codes, numerals, or patterns of dots."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Note: during the call there was some confusion between serial number and model number. We agreed that it would be very helpful for all those terms to have example of usages - please add if you have any :-)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: IAO"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "serial number"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000028.
cdao:IAO_0000132 cdao:IAO_0000111 "lot number"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A lot number is an information content entity which is an identical sequence of character borne by part of manufactured product or its packaging for each instances of a product class in a discrete batch of an item. Lot numbers are usually assigned to each separate production run of an item. Manufacturing as a lot might be due to a variety of reasons, for example,  a single process during which many individuals are made from the same portion of source material. Lot numbers can be encoded in a pattern  of other information objects, such as bar codes, numerals, or patterns of dots."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: IAO"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "batch number"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "lot number"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000028.
cdao:IAO_0000135 cdao:IAO_0000112 """The process of creation is, for example,  writing down on paper the name of a friend by deliberately creating a certain pattern using ink.

Here the ink + paper is the independent continuant and the carrier is the pattern in the ink.

c = pattern in the ink
b = paper + ink
r = friend""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """c specifically denotes r =def 
r is a portion of reality
& c is a particular quality
& c depends specifically on some independent continuant b 
& b acquired c as the result of the achievement of an objective to enable pointing to r repeatedly. 

Marked means there is a changed or additional quality of the bearer - the  quality is the information carrier.

Case 1
Memory trace as mark created when reading some description of some friend. The trace can denote.

Case 2
Pattern of ink arrayed on paper as mark when writing down a friend's name

Case 3
Pattern of magnetic domains on scattered pieces of a hard disk platter as mark when saving a file.""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "see https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/25&q=denote",
                                  "8/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: The suggestions is to deprecate specific and generically denotes in favor of a single denote relationship that corresponds to the generic sense";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Smith, Ceusters, Ruttenberg, 2000 years of philosophy";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_specifically denotes";
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000136 cdao:IAO_0000112 "This document is about information artifacts and their representations"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is_about is a (currently) primitive relation that relates an information artifact to an entity."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """7/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg. Following discussion with Jonathan Rees, and introduction of \"mentions\" relation. Weaken the is_about relationship to be primitive. 

We will try to build it back up by elaborating the various subproperties that are more precisely defined.

Some currently missing phenomena that should be considered \"about\" are predications - \"The only person who knows the answer is sitting beside me\" , Allegory, Satire, and other literary forms that can be topical without explicitly mentioning the topic."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Smith, Ceusters, Ruttenberg, 2000 years of philosophy"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:IAO_0000030;
                 rdfs:label "is about"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000140 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A settings datum is a datum that denotes some configuration of an instrument."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Alan grouped these in placeholder for the moment. Name by analogy to measurement datum."@en,
                                  """2/3/2009 Feedback from OBI

This should be a \"setting specification\". There is a question of whether it is information about a realizable or not.

Pro other specification are about realizables.
Cons sometimes specifies a quality which is not a realizable."""@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "setting datum"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000027.
cdao:IAO_0000141 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Need to rework digital entity. Digital quality was suggested by Barry.",
                                  "3/22/2009 Alan Ruttenberg, obsoleted per http://groups.google.com/group/information-ontology/browse_thread/thread/789ad4b7708d5cf4";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_digital quality";
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000142 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An information artifact IA mentions an entity E exactly when it has a component/part that denotes E"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """7/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: Add this relation following conversation with Jonathan Rees that N&S GCI for is_about was too strong. Really it was simply sufficient. To effect this change we introduce this relation, which is subproperty of is_about, and have previous GCI use this relation \"mentions\" in it's (logical) definition"""@en,
                                  "7/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg. P4 RC1 munges our GCI so remove it for now: mentions some entity equivalentTo has_part some ('generically denotes' some entity)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Jonathan Rees"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "mentions"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:IAO_0000136.
cdao:IAO_0000144 cdao:IAO_0000111 "conclusion textual entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "that fucoidan has a small statistically significant effect on AT3 level but no useful clinical effect as in-vivo anticoagulant, a paraphrase of part of the last paragraph of the discussion section of the paper 'Pilot clinical study to evaluate the anticoagulant activity of fucoidan', by Lowenthal et. al.PMID:19696660"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A textual entity that expresses the results of reasoning about a problem, for instance as typically found towards the end of scientific papers."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009/09/28 Alan Ruttenberg. Fucoidan-use-case"@en,
                                  "2009/10/23 Alan Ruttenberg: We need to work on the definition still"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "conclusion textual entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000338 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000312 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:IAO_0000300,
                                 cdao:OBI_0001909,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000027 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000124 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:IAO_0000178 cdao:IAO_0000111 "material information bearer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "a hard drive"@en,
                                  "A page of a paperback novel with writing on it. The paper itself is a material information bearer, the pattern of ink is the information carrier."@en,
                                  "a brain"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A material entity in which a concretization of an information content entity inheres."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: IAO"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "material information bearer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000040;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:BFO_0000040
                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000030 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>] ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000053 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:IAO_0000179 cdao:IAO_0000111 "histogram"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """A histogram is a report graph which is a statistical description of a
distribution in terms of occurrence frequencies of different event classes."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "PERSON:James Malone"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "histogram"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000180 cdao:IAO_0000111 "heatmap"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """A heatmap is a report graph which is a graphical representation of data
where the values taken by a variable(s) are shown as colors in a
two-dimensional map."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "PERSON:James Malone"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "heatmap"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000181 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Venn diagram"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """A Venn diagram is a report graph showing all hypothetically possible
logical relations between a finite collection of sets."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:James Malone"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venn_diagram"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Venn diagram"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000182 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolete_survival curve"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A survival curve is a report graph which is a graphical representation of data where the percentage of survival is plotted as a function of time."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:James Malone"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://www.graphpad.com/www/book/survive.htm"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_survival curve"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000183 cdao:IAO_0000111 "dendrogram"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """Dendrograms are often used in computational biology to
illustrate the clustering of genes."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """A dendrogram is a report graph which is a tree diagram
frequently used to illustrate the arrangement of the clusters produced by a
clustering algorithm."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:James Malone"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendrogram"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "dendrogram"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000184 cdao:IAO_0000111 "scatter plot"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Comparison of gene expression values in two samples can be displayed in a scatter plot"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A scatterplot is a graph which uses Cartesian coordinates to display values for two variables for a set of data. The data is displayed as a collection of points, each having the value of one variable determining the position on the horizontal axis and the value of the other variable determining the position on the vertical axis."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:James Malone"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "scattergraph"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scatterplot"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "scatter plot"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000038.
cdao:IAO_0000185 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A photograph is created by projecting an image onto a photosensitive surface such as a chemically treated plate or film, CCD receptor, etc."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Joanne Luciano"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photograph"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "photograph"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000101.
cdao:IAO_0000186 cdao:IAO_0000111 "photographic print"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A photographic print is a material entity upon which a photograph generically depends."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "photographic print"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000178;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:BFO_0000040
                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000185 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>] ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000053 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:IAO_0000219 cdao:IAO_0000112 """A person's name denotes the person. A variable name in a computer program denotes some piece of memory. Lexically equivalent strings can denote different things, for instance \"Alan\" can denote different people. In each case of use, there is a case of the denotation relation obtaining, between \"Alan\" and the person that is being named."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "denotes is a primitive, instance-level, relation obtaining between an information content entity and some portion of reality. Denotation is what happens when someone creates an information content entity E in order to specifically refer to something. The only relation between E and the thing is that E can be used to 'pick out' the thing. This relation connects those two together. Freedictionary.com sense 3: To signify directly; refer to specifically"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2009-11-10 Alan Ruttenberg. Old definition said the following to emphasize the generic nature of this relation. We no longer have 'specifically denotes', which would have been primitive, so make this relation primitive.
g denotes r =def 
r is a portion of reality
there is some c that is a concretization of g 
every c that is a concretization of g specifically denotes r"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Conversations with Barry Smith, Werner Ceusters, Bjoern Peters, Michel Dumontier, Melanie Courtot, James Malone, Bill Hogan"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:comment ""@en;
                 rdfs:label "denotes"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:IAO_0000136.
cdao:IAO_0000220 cdao:IAO_0000116 "see https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/25&q=denote";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_materially denotes";
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000221 cdao:IAO_0000115 """m is a quality measurement of q at t when
q is a quality 
there is a measurement process p that has specified output m, a measurement datum, that is about q"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details."""@en,
                                  """From the second IAO workshop [Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009: not completely current, though bringing in comparison is probably important]

This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details.
--
From the second IAO workshop, various comments, [commented on by Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009]

unit of measure is a quality, e.g. the length of a ruler.

[We decided to hedge on what units of measure are, instead talking about measurement unit labels, which are the information content entities that are about whatever measurement units are. For IAO we need that information entity in any case. See the term measurement unit label]

[Some struggling with the various subflavors of is_about. We subsequently removed the relation represents, and describes until and only when we have a better theory]

a represents b means either a denotes b or a describes

describe:
a describes b means a is about b and a allows an inference of at least one quality of b

We have had a long discussion about denotes versus describes."""@en,
                                  """From the second meeting on IAO:

An attempt at defining assay using Barry's \"reliability\" wording

assay:
process and has_input some material entity
and has_output some information content entity 
and which is such that instances of this process type reliably generate 
outputs that describes the input."""@en,
                                  """From the second IAO workshop: An attempt at tieing the quality to the measurement datum more carefully.

a is a magnitude means a is a determinate quality particular inhering in some bearer b existing at a time t that can be represented/denoted by an information content entity e that has parts denoting a unit of measure, a number, and b. The unit of measure is an instance of the determinable quality."""@en,
                                  "8/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: The strategy is to be rather specific with this relationship. There are other kinds of measurements that are not of qualities, such as those that measure time. We will add these as separate properties for the moment and see about generalizing later"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:IAO_0000109;
                 rdfs:label "is quality measurement of"@en;
                 rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000019;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:IAO_0000136;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:IAO_0000417];
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:IAO_0000417.
cdao:IAO_0000222 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_describes";
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000223 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_represents";
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000224 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Core is an instance of a grouping of terms from an ontology or ontologies. It is used by the ontology to identify main classes."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#Subset>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "core"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000225 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolescence reason specification"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The reason for which a term has been deprecated. The allowed values come from an enumerated list of predefined terms. See the specification of these instances for more detailed definitions of each enumerated value."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "The creation of this class has been inspired in part by Werner Ceusters' paper, Applying evolutionary terminology auditing to the Gene Ontology."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolescence reason specification"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000102;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#oneOf> (cdao:IAO_0000103
                                                                                                         cdao:IAO_0000226
                                                                                                         cdao:IAO_0000227
                                                                                                         cdao:IAO_0000228
                                                                                                         cdao:IAO_0000229) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:IAO_0000226 a cdao:IAO_0000225,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing>;
                 rdfs:label "placeholder removed"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000227 cdao:IAO_0000116 "An editor note should explain what were the merged terms and the reason for the merge."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000225,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "terms merged"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000228 cdao:IAO_0000116 "This is to be used when the original term has been replaced by a term imported from an other ontology. An editor note should indicate what is the URI of the new term to use."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000225,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "term imported"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000229 cdao:IAO_0000116 "This is to be used when a term has been split in two or more new terms. An editor note should indicate the reason for the split and indicate the URIs of the new terms created."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000225,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "term split"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000230 cdao:IAO_0000116 "We expect to be able to mine these new reasons and add instances as required."@en,
                                  "This is to be used if none of the existing instances cover the reason for obsolescence. An editor note should indicate this new reason."@en;
                 a cdao:IAO_0000225,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "other"@en;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has obsolescence reason"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Relates an annotation property to an obsolescence reason. The values of obsolescence reasons come from a list of predefined terms, instances of the class obsolescence reason specification."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                                  "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "has obsolescence reason"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000232 cdao:IAO_0000111 "curator note"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An administrative note of use for a curator but of no use for a user"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy cdao:iao.owl;
                 rdfs:label "curator note"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000233 cdao:IAO_0000111 "term tracker item";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "the URI for an OBI Terms ticket at sourceforge, such as https://sourceforge.net/p/obi/obi-terms/772/";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An IRI or similar locator for a request or discussion of an ontology term.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jie Zheng, Chris Stoeckert, Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Person: Jie Zheng, Chris Stoeckert, Alan Ruttenberg";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:comment "The 'tracker item' can associate a tracker with a specific ontology term.";
                 rdfs:label "term tracker item"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000234 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The name of the person, project, or organization that motivated inclusion of an ontology term by requesting its addition.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jie Zheng, Chris Stoeckert, Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Person: Jie Zheng, Chris Stoeckert, Alan Ruttenberg";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>;
                 rdfs:comment "The 'term requester' can credit the person, organization or project who request the ontology term.";
                 rdfs:label "ontology term requester"@en.
cdao:IAO_0000300 cdao:IAO_0000111 "textual entity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Words, sentences, paragraphs, and the written (non-figure) parts of publications are all textual entities"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A textual entity is a part of a manifestation (FRBR sense), a generically dependent continuant whose concretizations are patterns of glyphs intended to be interpreted as words, formulas, etc."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "AR, (IAO call 2009-09-01): a document as a whole is not typically a textual entity, because it has pictures in it - rather there are parts of it that are textual entities. Examples: The title, paragraph 2 sentence 7, etc."@en,
                                  "MC, 2009-09-14 (following IAO call 2009-09-01): textual entities live at the FRBR (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_Requirements_for_Bibliographic_Records) manifestation level. Everything is significant: line break, pdf and html versions of same document are different textual entities."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "text"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "textual entity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:IAO_0000301 cdao:IAO_0000111 "citation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Verspoor, K., Cohen, KB., Hunter, L. Textual characteristics of traditional and Open Access scientific journals are similar, BMC Bioinformatics 2009, 10:183."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a textual entity intended to identify a particular publication"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
