cdao:OBI_0000006 cdao:IAO_0000111 "role of being consumer safety officer";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Consumer safety officer; Consumer Safety Officer Positions at FDA http://69.20.19.211/jobs/cso.htm"@en,
                                  "Person charged with serving as CSO, FDA official who coordinates the review"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "the role of a human being that is realized by enforcing regulations to ensure consumer safety";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                                  "Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI, CDISC"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "role of being consumer safety officer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000273.
cdao:OBI_0000010 cdao:IAO_0000111 "fluorescent reporter intensity"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A measurement datum that represents the output of a scanner measuring the intensity value for each fluorescent reporter."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:OBI";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "From the DT branch: This term and definition were originally submitted by the community to our branch, but we thought they best fit DENRIE. However we see several issues with this. First of all the name 'probe' might not be used in OBI. Instead we have a 'reporter' role. Also, albeit the term 'probe intensity' is often used in communities such as the microarray one, the name 'probe' is ambiguous (some use it to refer to what's on the array, some use it to refer to what's hybed to the array). Furthermore, this concept could possibly be encompassed by combining different OBI terms, such as the roles of analyte, detector and reporter (you need something hybed to a probe on the array to get an intensity) and maybe a more general term for 'measuring intensities'. We need to find the right balance between what is consistent with OBI and combinations of its terms and what is user-friendly. Finally, note that 'intensity' is already in the OBI .owl file and is also in PATO. Why didn't OBI import it from PATO? This might be a problem."@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "fluorescent reporter intensity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000109.
cdao:OBI_0000011 cdao:IAO_0000111 "planned process",
                                  "planned process"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Injecting mice with a vaccine in order to test its efficacy";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A processual entity that realizes a plan which is the concretization of a plan specification."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """We are only considering successfully completed planned processes. A plan may be modified, and details added during execution. For a given planned process, the associated realized plan specification is the one encompassing all changes made during execution. This means that all processes in which an agent acts towards achieving some 
objectives is a planned process.""",
                                  "'Plan' includes a future direction sense. That can be problematic if plans are changed during their execution. There are however implicit contingencies for protocols that an agent has in his mind that can be considered part of the plan, even if the agent didn't have them in mind before. Therefore, a planned process can diverge from what the agent would have said the plan was before executing it, by adjusting to problems encountered during execution (e.g. choosing another reagent with equivalent properties, if the originally planned one has run out.)";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "branch derived";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "This class merges the previously separated objective driven process and planned process, as they the separation proved hard to maintain. (1/22/09, branch call)"@en,
                                  "6/11/9: Edited at workshop. Used to include: is initiated by an agent";
                 cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:obi.owl;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "planned process"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000015;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000104 ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>] ; 
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000055 ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000014 cdao:IAO_0000111 "regulator role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Fact sheet - Regulating the companies The role of the regulator. Ofwat is the economic regulator of the water and sewerage industry in England and Wales.  http://www.ofwat.gov.uk/aptrix/ofwat/publish.nsf/Content/roleofregulator_factsheet170805"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a regulatory role involved with making and/or enforcing relevant legislation and governmental orders"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "regulator";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "regulator role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000017.
cdao:OBI_0000015 cdao:IAO_0000111 "biological feature identification objective"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Biological_feature_identification_objective is an objective role carried out by the proposition defining the aim of a study designed to examine or characterize a particular biological feature."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "biological feature identification objective"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000005.
cdao:OBI_0000016 cdao:IAO_0000111 "regulation-assigned role"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Approval letter"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Regulation-assigned role is a regulatory role defined by legislation or governmental orders"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "regulation-assigned role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000017.
cdao:OBI_0000017 cdao:IAO_0000111 "regulatory role"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Regulatory agency, Ethics committee, Approval letter; example:  Browse these EPA Regulatory Role subtopics  http://www.epa.gov/ebtpages/enviregulatoryrole.html  Feb 29, 2008"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a role which inheres in material entities and is realized in the processes of making, enforcing or being defined by legislation or orders issued by a governmental body."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP:  Role branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI, CDISC"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "govt agents responsible for creating regulations; proxies for enforcing regulations.  CDISC definition:  regulatory authorities. Bodies having the power to regulate. NOTE: In the ICH GCP guideline the term includes the authorities that review submitted clinical data and those that conduct inspections. These bodies are sometimes referred to as competent"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "regulatory role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_0000018 cdao:IAO_0000111 "material supplier role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Jackson Labs is an organization which provide mice as experimental material";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a role realized through the process of supplying materials such as animal subjects, reagents or other materials used in an investigation."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Supplier role is a special kind of service, e.g. biobank";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "material provider role",
                                  "supplier";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "material supplier role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000947.
cdao:OBI_0000020 cdao:IAO_0000111 "contract research organization role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a worker role of carrying out the study according to the protocol document or study plan delivered by the PI, under the control of the study director.  This role cannot make decisions about the study execution"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "contract research organization";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "contract research organization role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000116.
cdao:OBI_0000021 cdao:IAO_0000111 "list-mode data file"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "An example of a list-mode data file is a file following list-mode Flow Cytometry Standard (FCS) format. Since FCS files can be in histogram mode or  list-mode we have to specify which data format specifically. List-mode format in the overwhelming (even universal) option used."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A list-mode data file is a binary digital entity where events are stored sequentially, parameter by parameter."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "One example of usage is in the context of flow cytometry, however is not restricted to this community and is more widely used, e.g. by imaging people."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:Flow Cytometry community";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "list-mode data file"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:OBI_0000023 cdao:IAO_0000111 "classified data set";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A data set that is produced as the output of a class prediction data transformation and consists of a data set with assigned class labels."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                                  "PERSON: Monnie McGee";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "data set with assigned class labels";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "classified data set"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000100;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000663 ; 
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000312 ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000025 cdao:IAO_0000111 "reference substance role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Calibration standard, positive control substance, vehicle   Good Laboratory Practices: Questions and Answers - Test Control and Reference Substance Characterization  http://www.epa.gov/enforcement/monitoring/programs/fifra/glpqanda-character.html"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a role inhering in a material entity that is realized when  characteristics or responses elicited by the substance are used for comparison or reference."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "reference substance";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "reference substance role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000040 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000052 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_0000026 cdao:IAO_0000111 "cytological stain role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "haemotoxylin is a general purpose nuclear stain extracted from the wood of the logwood tree WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haematoxylin";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A dye role that is realized when the stain is used to colour cells and or cellular components for the purposes of visualization";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                                  "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "cytological stain";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "cytological stain role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000250.
cdao:OBI_0000029 cdao:IAO_0000111 "centrifuge pellet role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Definition of pellet :the material concentrated at the bottom of a centrifuge tube after centrifugation. http://www.everythingbio.com/glos/definition.php?word=pellet";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "pellet role is a role which inheres in a material entity and is realized by a material separation process using gravitational force generated by a centrifuge in which the material bearing the pellet role is the heavier or heaviest component of the output material.."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP:  Role branch";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "9Mar09 after discussion with process branch changed definition to include use of centrifuge;";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "centrifuge pellet role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0302886 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000054 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000040 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000052 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_0000032 cdao:IAO_0000111 "clinical research coordinator role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a worker role comprised of handling the administrative duties of a trial or study."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "clinical research coordinator";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "clinical research coordinator role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000116.
cdao:OBI_0000034 cdao:IAO_0000111 "supernatant role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Precipitation is the formation of a solid in a solution during a chemical reaction. When the reaction occurs, the solid formed is called the precipitate, and the liquid remaining above the solid is called the supernate.  Wikipedia";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "supernatant role is a role which inheres in a material entity and is realized by a material separation process using gravitational force in which the material bearing the supernatant role is the liquid component of the output material.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "GROUP: Role branch";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "supernatant role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0600014 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000054 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000040 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000052 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_0000038 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromatography column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Chromatography column in chemistry is a tube and contents (typically glass) used to purify individual chemical compounds from mixtures of compounds. It is often used for preparative applications on scales from micrograms up to kilograms."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Column_chromatography"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "open tracker https://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?func=detail&aid=2881353&group_id=177891&atid=886178";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chromatography column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:OBI_0000372
                                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0600046 ; 
