cdao:OBI_0000154 cdao:IAO_0000111 "role of Institutional Review Board";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "An institutional review board/independent ethics committee (IRB/IEC) (also known as ethical review board) is a group that has been formally designated to approve, monitor, and review biomedical and behavioral research involving humans with the alleged aim to protect the rights and welfare of the subjects.  Wikipedia March 2008"@en,
                                  "Animal protocol review board";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "the role of a organization that is realized by members reviewing study designs for their agreement with regulations";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                                  "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "Internal Review Board";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI, CDISC"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "CDISC definition:  institutional review board; independent ethics committee (IEC). An independent body (a review board or a committee, institutional, regional, national, or supranational) constituted of medical/scientific professionals and non-scientific members, whose responsibility it is to ensure the protection of the rights, safety and well-being of human subjects involved in a trial."@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "role of Institutional Review Board"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000014.
cdao:OBI_0000158 cdao:IAO_0000111 "eSource document"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "an eSource document is a digital document consisting of a logical collection of Source data and other eSource documents that can be presented in an ordered way and capture the time of completion, change, and any signatures"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "article-without-pmid-or-doi:CDISCglossary";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "eSource document"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:OBI_0000161 cdao:IAO_0000111 "crossover population role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a role realized when a participant serves as reference to itself";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "crossover population";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "crossover population role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000220.
cdao:OBI_0000162 cdao:IAO_0000111 "complete nutrient role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Rat chow; RPMI medium + serum; use example:  CNS17 (Complete Nutrient System) Grow 3-2-4, http://www.kalyx.com/store/proddetail.cfm/ItemID/552307/CategoryID/12000/SubCatID/2755/file.htm"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A nutrient role that inheres in a material entity and is realized in the use of that material entity by an organism to provide all needed nourishment.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "complete nutrient";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "complete nutrient role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000204.
cdao:OBI_0000163 cdao:IAO_0000111 "radiolabel role"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a molecular label role which inheres in a material entity which is realized by the process of radioactivity detection"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "radiolabel"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "radiolabel role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:REO_0000171.
cdao:OBI_0000164 cdao:IAO_0000111 "cDNA library"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID:6110205. collection of cDNA derived from mouse splenocytes."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """Mixed population of cDNAs (complementaryDNA) made from mRNA from a defined source, usually a specific cell type. This term should be associated only to nucleic acid interactors not to their proteins product. For instance in 2h screening use living cells (MI:0349) as sample process.

ALT DEF (PRS):: a cDNA library is a collection of host cells, typically E.Coli cells but not exclusively. modified by transfer of plasmid DNA molecule used as vector containing a fragment or totality of cDNA molecule (the insert) .  cDNA library may have an array of role and applications."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Luisa Montecchi"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: PSI"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 """PRS: 22022008. class moved under population,
modification of definition and replacement of biomaterials in previous definition with 'material'
addition of has_role restriction"""@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "cDNA library"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000731 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000643 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000731,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0600064 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000312 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000167 cdao:IAO_0000111 "electronic case report form"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An electronic case report form is a digital document used to record all of the protocol required information to be reported for each trial subject. An eCRF has the property that it can be audited and compliant with requirements of 21 CFR Part 11."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "CDISC glossary";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "electronic case report form"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:OBI_0000169 cdao:IAO_0000111 "placebo role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Pill consisting of inert materials"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a negative reference substance is a reference role in which the substance playing the reference substance role is physically similar in appearance to the test substance";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "placebo";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "CDISC definition placebo. A pharmaceutical preparation that does not contain the investigational agent. In blinded studies, it is generally prepared to be physically indistinguishable from the preparation containing the investigational product."@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "placebo role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000214.
cdao:OBI_0000171 cdao:IAO_0000111 "autotransplantation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is the transplantation of tissue from one part of \\nthe body to another in the same individual. )"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "autotransplantation"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000105.
cdao:OBI_0000172 cdao:IAO_0000111 "parameter threshold"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "0.01, 0.03"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A measurement datum measuring the minimal signal that must be detected to generate an electrical event, as compared to the maximal detected signal in a flow cytometer instrument. The datum has a qualitative role"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Kevin Clancy"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Submitted by the Flow Cytometry community in DigitalEntity-FlowCytometry-2007-03-30.txt";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "parameter threshold"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000109.
cdao:OBI_0000174 cdao:IAO_0000111 "study group role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The group of randomized participants that are assigned to a treatment arm of the trial";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a study population role where the bearer is a population of material entities and the role is realized in the implementation of a study design wherein the entities bearing the study population role are observed or subjected to intervention according to the study design and are biological replicates, i.e. they receive the same treatment under the protocol"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "study group population";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "study group role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_0000175 cdao:IAO_0000111 "p-value"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """PMID:19696660
in contrast to the in-vivo data AT-III increased significantly from
113.5% at baseline to 117% after 4 days (n = 10, P-value= 0.02; Table 2).""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000121;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A quantitative confidence value that represents the probability of obtaining a result at least as extreme as that actually obtained, assuming that the actual value was the result of chance alone."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "May be outside the scope of OBI long term, is needed so is retained";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P-value";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "p-value"@en;
