cdao:OBI_0000196 cdao:IAO_0000111 "role of impartial witness";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """According to GCP , an impartial witness should be present for an
illiterate subject. PharmPK Discussion, http://www.boomer.org/pkin/PK06/PK2006253.html"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a role which inheres in a Homo sapiens and is realized during a clinical trial - the impartial witness is independent of the trial and cannot be unfairly influenced by people involved with the trial";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "impartial witness. A person, who is independent of the trial, who cannot be unfairly influenced by people involved with the trial, who attends the informed consent process if the subject or the subject's legally acceptable representative cannot read, and who"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en,
                                  "Person: Helen Parkinson";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "impartial witness";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "role of impartial witness"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000016.
cdao:OBI_00001975 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromatin immunoprecipitation"@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000112 "Yang et al, Int J Clin Exp Pathol. 2015; 8(3): 2746–275 PMID:26045780. Cells were lysed and sonicated to shear DNA to lengths between 200-1000 bp. The sample was then incubated with antibodies against Acety-H3 to immunoprecipitate protein-DNA complexes using protein A agarose beads. The isolated protein-DNA complexes were treated with proteinase K digestion to remove histones. QPCR was then performed using primers specific for TGF-β1, MMP-9 and PI3K promoters at 95°C for 5 min, followed by 40 cycles at 95 °C for 20 s, 58°C for 20 s, and 72°C for 20 s. Each QPCR reaction was repeated in triplicate. QPCR was followed by a melt curve analysis to determine the reaction specificity. The relative gene expression was calculated using 2-ΔΔCt method."@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                  cdao:IAO_0000115 "An immunoprecipitation in which chromatin (i.e. packaged DNA which can include protein and RNA complexes) is cut into short regions, reversibly cross linked, and antibodies or tags are used to select for pieces of chromatin with desired characteristics."@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters, Randi Vita, James A. Overton"@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000118 "ChIP"@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI"@en;
                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                  rdfs:label "chromatin immunoprecipitation"@en;
                  rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000690.
cdao:OBI_0000198 cdao:IAO_0000111 "biological replicate role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "A member of a dose-time group; a patient in a given arm of a trial"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a reference participant role realized by equivalent treatment of participants";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
