cdao:OBI_0000213 cdao:IAO_0000111 "fluorescence compensation matrix"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "((1.053096, -0.22476), (-0.24877, 1.053096))"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A fluorescence compensation matrix is a square matrix which is used as the left multiplier of the vector of fluorescence values while performing digital fluorescence compensation. Also, fluorescence compensation matrix is the inverse of the fluorescence spillover matrix."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Chris Stoeckert"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "group:Flow Cytometry community";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "fluorescence compensation matrix"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000030.
cdao:OBI_0000214 cdao:IAO_0000111 "negative reference substance role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Saline solution"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """a reference role in which the characteristics or responses elicited by the substance playing the reference substance role are used to establish a \"no effect\" response""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "negative reference substance";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
