                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Patterns of benzylpiperazine/trifluoromethylphenylpiperazine party pill use and adverse effects in a population sample in New Zealand. Drug Alcohol Rev. 2008 Mar 31:1-7.  PMID: 18608458"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A sample population is an object aggregate that is selected from the population, e.g. the fish in the net that were sampled from the lake, the people that responded to the call for volunteers."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "03/21/2010: BP, obsoleting this term, as it is duplicated by 'material sample'. Use that instead term instead, which now also has 'sample population' as an alternative label.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel",
                                  "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "recruited population"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial Branch";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000227;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_sample population"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000268 cdao:IAO_0000111 "organism feature identification objective"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Organism_feature_identification_objective is a biological_feature_identification_objective role describing a study designed to examine or characterize a biological feature monitored at the level of the organism, e.g. height, weight, stage of development, stage of life cycle."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "organism feature identification objective"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000015.
cdao:OBI_0000269 cdao:IAO_0000111 "number of lost events computer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "0, 125, 787 events lost due to computer busy."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A measurement datum recording the number of measurement events lost due to overloading of the analysis chip in a flow cytometer instrument. The datum has a qualitative role"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Kevin Clancy"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Submitted by the Flow Cytometry community in DigitalEntity-FlowCytometry-2007-03-30.txt";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "number of lost events computer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000109.
cdao:OBI_0000272 cdao:IAO_0000111 "protocol"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PCR protocol, has objective specification, amplify DNA fragment of interest, and has action specification describes the amounts of experimental reagents used (e..g. buffers, dNTPS, enzyme), and the temperature and cycle time settings for running the PCR."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A plan specification which has sufficient level of detail and quantitative information to communicate it between investigation agents, so that different investigation agents will reliably be able to independently reproduce the process."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived + wikipedia (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protocol_%28natural_sciences%29)"@en;
                 cdao:OBI_0001847 "study protocol";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "protocol"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000104.
cdao:OBI_0000273 cdao:IAO_0000111 "role of regulator of consumables and medical devices";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "FDA, EMEA; http://www.fda.gov/; The International Conference of Drug Regulatory Authorities (ICDRAs) provide drug regulatory authorities of WHO Member States with a forum to meet and discuss ways to strengthen collaboration.http://www.who.int/medicines/areas/quality_safety/regulation_legislation/icdra/en/index.html"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a regulator involved with making and enforcing legislation and governmental orders relevant to the development, testing, manufacture and use of food, drugs and medical devices"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "drug regulatoy authority";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI, CDISC"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "role of regulator of consumables and medical devices"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000014.
cdao:OBI_0000274 cdao:IAO_0000111 "adding a material entity into a target";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Injecting a drug into a mouse. Adding IL-2 to a cell culture. Adding NaCl into water.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is a process with the objective to place a material entity bearing the 'material to be added role' into a material bearing the 'target of material addition role'."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "Class was renamed from 'administering substance', as this is commonly used only for additions into organisms.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "BP";
