cdao:OBI_0000292 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has_feature_value";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "has_feature_value datatype property is used to describe the feature values which the feature class can contain, for example has_base can have feature values of nonNegativeInteger values."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "James Malone"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:OBI_0200140;
                 rdfs:label "has_feature_value"@en.
cdao:OBI_0000293 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has_specified_input",
                                  "has_specified_input"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "see is_input_of example_of_usage"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A relation between a planned process and a continuant participating in that process that is not created during  the process. The presence of the continuant during the process is explicitly specified in the plan specification which the process realizes the concretization of."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "8/17/09: specified inputs of one process are not necessarily specified inputs of a larger process that it is part of. This is in contrast to how 'has participant' works.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Larry Hunter",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters",
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Melanie Coutot";
                 cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:obi.owl;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:OBI_0000011;
                 rdfs:label "has_specified_input"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000057;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:OBI_0000295];
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:OBI_0000295.
cdao:OBI_0000294 cdao:IAO_0000111 "is_concretization_of";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Is a relationship between a generically dependent continuant and a specifically dependent continuant. A generically dependent continuant may inhere in more than one entity. It does so by virtue of the fact that there is, for each entity that it inheres, a specifically dependent *concretization* of the generically dependent continuant that is specifically dependent. For instance, consider a story, which is an information artifact that inheres in some number of books. Each book bears some quality that carries the story. The relation between this quality and the generically dependent continuant is that the former is the concretization of the latter.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "replaced by: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000058";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenburg",
                                  "PERSON: Barry Smith";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_is_concretization_of"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000295 cdao:IAO_0000111 "is_specified_input_of";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "some Autologous EBV(Epstein-Barr virus)-transformed B-LCL (B lymphocyte cell line) is_input_for instance of Chromum Release Assay described at https://wiki.cbil.upenn.edu/obiwiki/index.php/Chromium_Release_assay"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A relation between a planned process and a continuant participating in that process that is not created during  the process. The presence of the continuant during the process is explicitly specified in the plan specification which the process realizes the concretization of."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Bjoern Peters",
                                  "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "is_specified_input_of"@en;
                 rdfs:range cdao:OBI_0000011;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000056;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:OBI_0000293].
cdao:OBI_0000296 cdao:IAO_0000111 "enrollment"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """Enrollment of patients in a study.
Short-term outcome of neuropsychiatric events in systemic lupus erythematosus upon enrollment into an international inception cohort study. Arthritis Rheum. 2008 May 15;59(5):721-9. PMID: 18438902"""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "enrollment is a process of identifying a set of objects for further use in an investigation based on a set of criteria or rules"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "merged with 'enrollment of human subjects";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "IEDB"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000227;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_enrollment"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000297 cdao:IAO_0000111 "is_concretized_as";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Is a relationship between a specifically dependent continuant and a generically dependent continuant. A generically dependent continuant may inhere in more than one entity. It does so by virtue of the fact that there is, for each entity that it inheres, a specifically dependent *concretization* of the generically dependent continuant that is specifically dependent. For instance, consider a story, which is an information artifact that inheres in some number of books. Each book bears some quality that carries the story. The relation between this quality and the generically dependent continuant is that the former is the concretization of the latter.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "replaced by: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000059";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Barry Smith",
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_is_concretized_as"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000298 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has_quality";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """A relation between an entity and a quality. For types: E has_quality Q iff: 
for any eEt, exists qQt such that q inheres_in e at t. 
For instances: e has_quality q at t iff q inheres_in e at t and q instance-of Quality [GOC:cjm]""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "replaced by: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000086";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Mungall",
                                  "GROUP:OBI:<http://obi.sourceforge.net>";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_has_quality"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000299 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has_specified_output"@en,
                                  "has_specified_output";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A relation between a planned process and a continuant participating in that process. The presence of the continuant at the end of the process is explicitly specified in the objective specification which the process realizes the concretization of."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters",
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                                  "PERSON: Larry Hunter";
                 cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:obi.owl;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:domain cdao:OBI_0000011;
                 rdfs:label "has_specified_output"@en;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000057;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:OBI_0000312];
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:OBI_0000312.
