                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "OWL is a format standard of a digital entity that is conformant with the W3C Web Ontology Language specification.(http://www.w3.org/2004/OWL/)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "person:Jennifer Fostel"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "web-page:http://www.w3.org/2004/OWL/";
                 a cdao:IAO_0000098,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                 rdfs:label "OWL"@en.
cdao:OBI_0000338 cdao:IAO_0000111 "interpreting data";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Concluding that a gene is upregulated in a tissue sample based on the band intensity in a western blot.  Concluding that a patient has a infection based on measurement of an elevated body temperature and reported headache. Concluding that there were problems in an investigation because data from PCR and microarray are conflicting. Concluding that 'defects in gene XYZ cause cancer due to improper DNA repair' based on data from experiments in that study that gene XYZ is involved in DNA repair, and the conclusion of a previous study that cancer patients have an increased number of mutations in this gene. ";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A planned process in which data gathered in an investigation is evaluated in the context of existing knowledge with the objective to generate more general conclusions or to conclude that the data does not allow one to draw general conclusion"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Bjoern Peters";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "drawing a conclusion based on data"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0001909 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000011,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000027 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000339 cdao:IAO_0000111 "planning";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """The process of a scientist thinking about and deciding what reagents to use as part of a protocol for an experiment. Note that the scientist could be human or a \"robot scientist\" executing software.""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a process of creating or modifying a plan specification"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "7/18/2011 BP: planning used to itself be a planned process. Barry Smith pointed out that this would lead to an infinite regression, as there would have to be a plan to conduct a planning process, which in itself would be the result of planning etc. Therefore, the restrictions on 'planning' were loosened to allow for informal processes that result in an 'ad hoc plan '. This required changing from 'has_specified_output some plan specifiction' to 'has_participant some plan specification'. ";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Bjoern Peters",
                                  "Plans and Planned Processes Branch";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "planning"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000015,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:BFO_0000015
                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:IAO_0000104 ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000057 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0000340 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolete_documenting";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Recording the current temperature in a laboratory notebook. Writing a journal article. Updating a patient record in a database.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "6/11/9: Edited at workshop. Should go into IAO. We need to be able identify a child form of information artifact which corresponds to something enduring (not brain like). This used to be restricted to physical document or digital entity as the output, but that excludes e.g. an audio cassette tape";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "wikipedia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Documenting";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 cdao:IAO_0100001 "IAO_0000572";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_documenting"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000341 cdao:IAO_0000111 "histological sample preparation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "histological sample preparation is the preparation of an input tissue via slicing and labeling to make tissue microstructure of interest visible in a future histology assay"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Bjoern Peters"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "histological sample preparation"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000094,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0400168 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000057 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000456 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100066 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000684 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000659.
cdao:OBI_0000343 cdao:IAO_0000111 "inductive reasoning";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Based on the observation that all lung cancer patients treated with aspirin in our clinical trial survived longer than the control group, we conclude by inductive reasining that aspirin has a therapeutic effect on lung cancer."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000428;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a interpreting data that is used to ascribe properties or relations to types based on an observation instance (i.e., on a number of observations or experiences); or to formulate laws based on limited observations of recurring phenomenal patterns."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """BP: 10/22/122: After changing the parent class to drawing a conclusion *based on data* it is no longer clear that this class is needed; minimally it needs a better definition to distinguish it. 

Proposal is to obsolete. 

""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inductive_reasoning";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "inductive reasoning"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000338.
cdao:OBI_0000345 cdao:IAO_0000111 "mass analyzer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The mass analyzer of the Voyager-DE(tm) STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A Mass analyzer is a device that separates ions according to their mass-to-charge ratio. All mass spectrometers are based on dynamics of charged particles in electric and magnetic fields in vacuum where the two laws of Lorentz force law and Newton's second law of motion apply."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                                  "PERSON: Daniel Schober";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Mass_analyzer";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "mass analyzer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000932,
                                 cdao:OBI_0000832,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000372 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000355 cdao:IAO_0000111 "hypothesis driven investigation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is an investigation with the goal to test one or more hypothesis"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "hypothesis driven investigation"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000066.
cdao:OBI_0000356 cdao:IAO_0000111 "hypothesis generating investigation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is an investigation in which data is generated and analyzed with the purpose of generating new hypothesis"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "hypothesis generating investigation"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000066.
cdao:OBI_0000361 cdao:IAO_0000111 "ion source"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The ion source of a Voyager-DE??? STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """An ion source is a device that is part of a mass
spectrometer that ionizes the material under analysis. The ions are
then transported by magnetic or electric fields to the mass analyzer.
Techniques for ionization have been key to determining what types of
samples can be analyzed by mass spectrometry. Electron ionization and
chemical ionization are used for gases and vapors. In chemical
ionization sources, the material is ionized by chemical ion-molecule
reactions during collisions in the source. Two techniques often used
with liquid and solid biological samples include electrospray
ionization (due to John Fenn PMID 2675315.) and matrix-assisted laser
desorption/ionization (MALDI, due to M. Karas and F. Hillenkamp
(Measuring Mass: From Positive Rays to Proteins by Michael A. Grayson
(Editor) (ISBN 0-941901-31-9)))."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Ion_source";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "ion source"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000385 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000968.
cdao:OBI_0000364 cdao:IAO_0000111 "ion detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The ion detector of the Voyager-DE(tm) STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """An ion detector is a device that measures and records
the charge induced or current produced when an ion passes by or hits a
surface. 

Example: In a scanning instrument the signal produced in the detector
during the course of the scan versus where the instrument is in the
scan (at what m/Q) will produce a mass spectrum, a record of ions as a
function of m/Q."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Detector";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "ion detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000832.
cdao:OBI_0000365 cdao:IAO_0000111 "obsolete_results_from";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """2009/11/23: BP, dev call:o bsoleted as discussed in tracker https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&aid=2899860&group_id=177891&atid=886178
. Should be replaced by instead creating defined classes for materials, which are specified output of the process that conveys the""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_results_from";
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteProperty>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0000366 cdao:IAO_0000111 "metabolite profiling assay";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Metabolite profiling of human colon carcinoma - deregulation of TCA cycle and amino acid turnover. Mol Cancer. 2008 Sep 18;7(1):72. PMID: 18799019";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An assay that detects and identifies chemical entities resulting from biochemical and cellular metabolism";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "metabolite assay";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "metabolite profiling assay";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000070,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100051 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000367 cdao:IAO_0000111 "light emission function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A light emission function is an excitation function to excite a material to a specific excitation state that it emits light."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Melanie Courtot";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "light emission function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000374.
cdao:OBI_0000368 cdao:IAO_0000111 "record function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A record function is a function that registers or collects information in a particular format on a particular recording medium. For example on paper or a digital representation"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bill Bug",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "record function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000369 cdao:IAO_0000111 "magnify function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A magnify function is a function to increase the size of a transmitted object image through the precise arrangement of energy diffraction elements along an imaging path."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "magnify function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000370 cdao:IAO_0000111 "contain function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "A syringe, a beaker";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A contain function is a function to constrain a material entities location in space"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Daniel Schober";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "contain function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000371 cdao:IAO_0000111 "heat function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A heat function is a function that increases the internal kinetic energy of a material"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bill Bug",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "heat function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000372 cdao:IAO_0000111 "material separation function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A material separation function is a function that increases the resolution between two or more material entities. The  to distinction between the entities is usually based on some associated physical quality."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "material separation function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000373 cdao:IAO_0000111 "ionize process";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Electrospray ionization in mass spectrometry";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a physical process of converting an atom or molecule into an ion by adding or removing charged particles such as electrons or other ions. This excludes chemical processes of dissociation.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009-11-10. Tracker: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionize";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Bjoern Peters";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "ionize process"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000385 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000055 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000094,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:BFO_0000002 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000057 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000456 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000374 cdao:IAO_0000111 "excitation function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A excitation function is a function  to inject energy by bombarding a material with energetic particles (e.g., photons) thereby imbuing internal material components such as electrons with additional energy.  These internal, 'excited' particles may lead to the rupturing of covalent chemical bonds or may quickly relax back to there unexcited state with an exponential time course thereby locally emitting energy in the form of photons."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bill Bug",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "excitation function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000375 cdao:IAO_0000111 "freeze function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A freeze function is a function to decrease the internal kinetic energy of a material below the freezing point of that type of material."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Bill Bug";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "freeze function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000376 cdao:IAO_0000111 "synthesizing function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A synthesizing function is a function to assemble new output materials from distinct input materials.  The output materials typically consist of chemically distinct monomeric objects or object aggregate polymers.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Bill Bug";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "synthesizing function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000377 cdao:IAO_0000111 "perturb function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A perturb function is a function that disrupts the normal function of a system induced through either internal or external means.  External means of perturbation include: (1) displacement fields in the physical sense - e.g., temperature change, osmotic shock, pressure change; (2) application of small molecules such as drugs or toxins to perturb the function of specific pathways or application of surfactants to perturb the normal function of plasma membrane.  Internal means of perturbation include: (1) manipulation of gene function via gene knockout or transcript knockdown via RNAi; (2) directed genetic mutation leading to minimal aa alterations that interfere with peptide function."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Bill Bug";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perturbation_biology"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "perturb function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000378 cdao:IAO_0000111 "filter function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A filter function is a function to prevent the flow of certain entities based on a quality or qualities of the entity while allowing entities which have different qualities to pass through"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "filter function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000372.
cdao:OBI_0000379 cdao:IAO_0000111 "mechanical function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A mechanical function is a function that is realised via mechanical work (through an certain amount of energy transferred by some force)."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Melanie Courtot";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_work"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "mechanical function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000380 cdao:IAO_0000111 "gas filter function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A gas filter function is a filter function which prevents the flow of solid objects, defined by specific qualities, in a gas-solid mixture"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "gas filter function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000378.
cdao:OBI_0000381 cdao:IAO_0000111 "liquid filter function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A liquid filter function is a filter function which prevents the flow of solid objects, defined by specific qualities, in a liquid-solid mixture"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "liquid filter function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000378.
cdao:OBI_0000383 cdao:IAO_0000111 "transfer function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A transfer function is a function to displace a material from one location to another."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "transfer function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000384 cdao:IAO_0000111 "electricity supply function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "the function of supplying current during a neuroscience experiment.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An electricity supply function is an energy supply function to transfer electricity from one source to another, typically a consumer of the electricity or as a stimulus during a neuroscience experiment."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Daniel Schober";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "power supply"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "electricity supply function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000391.
cdao:OBI_0000385 cdao:IAO_0000111 "ionization function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "The ion source in amass spectrometer";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An ionization function is a function to physically convert an atom or molecule into an ion by adding or removing charged particles such as electrons or other ions."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Bill Bug",
                                  "Frank Gibson";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionization"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "ionization function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000387 cdao:IAO_0000111 "cool function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A cool function is a function to decrease the internal kinetic energy of a material below the initial kinetic energy of that type of material."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Daniel Schober";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "cool function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000388 cdao:IAO_0000111 "connection function"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "An electricity cable";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A connection function is a function to couple two or more flow channels so that material or signals can be transported from one set of channels to another."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bill Bug",
                                  "Daniel Schober",
                                  "Frank Gibson",
                                  "Melanie Courtot";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "connection function"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000034.
cdao:OBI_0000389 cdao:IAO_0000111 "isoelectric focusing device"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An isoelectric focusing device is a device in which isoelectric focusing can be performed. An isoelectric focussing device had the function to contain and control the contained environment and transfer electrical energy from a power supply to a separation medium and the charged material to be separated."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Frank Gibson";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "isoelectric focusing unit"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "sep:00097";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "isoelectric focusing device"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000401 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
