cdao:OBI_0000463 cdao:IAO_0000111 "column chromatography detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "There is a wide range of detectors available for both GC and LC each having their own particular areas of application. In general the more catholic the response, the less sensitive the detector and the most sensitive detectors are those that have a specific response. The performance of all detectors should be properly specified so that the user can determine which is most suitable for a specific application. Such specifications are also essential to compare the performance of different detectors supplied by alternative instrument manufactures. Detector specifications should be presented in a standard form and in standard units, so that detectors can be compared that function on widely different principles."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01077",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/Principles/Basic-Chromatograph/Detector/rs56.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "chromatography detector, defined class/xps"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "column chromatography detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000832,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000464 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker autosampler"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A Bruker autosampler is an autosampler made by Bruker."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400209",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker autosampler"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000555.
cdao:OBI_0000465 cdao:IAO_0000111 "organic acid column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An organic acid column is a chromatography column which enables (reversed-phase) separation of hydrophilic aliphatic and aromatic organic acids with UV detection. Organic acid columns allow retention of polar and apolar organic acids and are hydrolysis resistant."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01099",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "organic acid column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000466 cdao:IAO_0000111 "thermal conductivity detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The most commonly used detector in preparative GC is the thermal conductivity detector (hot wire detector). Even this detector, however, is often too sensitive and has too high a flow impedance. Under such circumstances, the procedure mentioned above must be employed. The eluent from the preparative column is split and a small portion diverted through the detector (sometimes with further dilution with carrier gas to reduce sensitivity)."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "TCD, hot wire detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01084",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/Preparative/Apparatus/Detectors/rs27.html>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "thermal conductivity detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000637.
cdao:OBI_0000467 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker US 2 NMR magnet"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An actively-shielded superconducting magnet from Bruker that combines Bruker BioSpin's advanced, proprietary UltraShield active shielding and UltraStabilized sub-cooling technologies. This shielded and stabilized (US2) magnet system delivers high sensitivity and spectral dispersion."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400189",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/nmr_magnets_950us2.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker US 2 NMR magnet"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000597.
cdao:OBI_0000468 cdao:IAO_0000111 "protein column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A protein column is a chromatography column used for the separation of complex protein mixtures. Protein columns enable sample desalting, followed by chromatographic separation or fractionation of complex protein samples, e.g. immunodepleted serum or plasma proteins."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01238",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "refactor as defined class"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "protein column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000469 cdao:IAO_0000111 "solvent mixer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A liquid chromatography device that mixes different solvents, e.g. under high pressure and in differrent volumes ranging from 5 ml to 5 L capacity. Powerful magnetic mixers provide vigorous agitation required for high pressure reaction chemistry."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01072";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "check on definition !"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "solvent mixer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000485.
cdao:OBI_0000470 cdao:IAO_0000111 "mass spectrometry assay";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Identification of a proteins cut out from a 2D gel by cleaving it into peptides using trypsin digestion using electrospray ionizatino to ensure the peptides are charged, and accelerating them with an electro magnetic field in which the flight path is determined by the mass / charge ratio of the peptides. Comparing the mass/charge ratio of peptides in the proteins with databases of protein sequences allows to identify which protein gave rise to the peptides.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An assay that identifies the amount and type of material entities present in a sample by fragmenting the sample and measuring the mass-to-charge ratio of the resulting particles.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "mass spectrometry assay";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000070,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> ([<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:BFO_0000034
                                                                                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000049 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000052 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>] ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000055 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]
                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000049 ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0000471 cdao:IAO_0000111 "study design execution";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "injecting a mouse with PBS solution, weighing it, and recording the weight according to a study design.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a planned process that carries out a study design";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "removed axiom has_part some (assay or 'data transformation') per discussion on protocol application mailing list to improve reasoner performance. The axiom is still desired.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "branch derived";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "6/11/9: edited at workshop. Used to be: study design execution is a process with the objective to generate data according to a concretized study design. The execution of a study design is part of an investigation, and minimally consists of an assay or data transformation.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:obi.owl;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "study design execution";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000011;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:OBI_0000011
                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0500000 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>] ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000055 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0000473 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker NMR Case sample changer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The NMR Case is an economical NMR sample changer for laboratories with modest automation needs. It expands the maximum number of samples your spectrometer can process during unattended operation to 24. The NMR Case consists of multiple components. The NMR Case exchange module installed atop your cryostat. The two front legs are adjustable, making the NMR Case compatible with many different cryostats."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400203",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/automation.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker NMR Case sample changer"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000464.
cdao:OBI_0000474 cdao:IAO_0000111 "nano pump system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A pump system optimized for nano flow chromatography."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01052",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "nano pump system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000589.
cdao:OBI_0000475 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker AutoClean system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "NMR tubes are often used once and discarded, creating needless waste. With the Bruker BioSpin Autoclean system you can now recycle 5mm, 3mm, or 5mm/3mm step-down (Wilmad 520-1B) NMR tubes. AutoClean NMR Tube Washing System is a simple way to recoup the substantial investment your organization makes in quality NMR tubes, and cut back on needless waste material."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "washing system/NMR tube washing system, XPS: device has function washing"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400205",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.used-line.com/c5983250s10028-Bruker_Biospin_NMR_Autoclean_Nuclear_Magnetic_Resonance_Organic_Solvents.htm>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker AutoClean system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000498.
cdao:OBI_0000476 cdao:IAO_0000111 "manual injection system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The traditional hardware system that allows a human to inject a sample into an inlet by hand, using a syringe."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01064",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "manual injection system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000504.
cdao:OBI_0000477 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Varian GEMINI spectrometer"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An older Varian Broadband NMR spectrometer."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
