cdao:OBI_0000481 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromatography detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A chromatography detector is a device that locates in the dimensions of space and time, the positions of the components of a mixture that has been subjected to a chromatographic process and thus permits the senses to appreciate the nature of the separation.  Defining characteristics are Dynamic Range, Response Index or Linearity, Linear Dynamic range, Detector Response,  Detector Noise Level, Detector Sensitivity or Minimum Detectable Concentration, Total System Dispersion, Sensor Dimensions, Detector Time Constant, Pressure Sensitivity, Flow Sensitivity, Operating Temperature Range."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01012",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/GC-Detectors/Classification/rs1.html>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chromatography detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000485.
cdao:OBI_0000482 cdao:IAO_0000111 "normal phase column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A normal phase column is a chromatography column in which the stationary phase is more polar than the mobile phase. Its counterpart is the reversed phase column."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01097",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "normal phase column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000483 cdao:IAO_0000111 "APOLLO console"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The APOLLO is a compact, modular, multiple-DSP, Windows XP Professional-based console that can be equipped with up to 8 DDS-based RF transmitter channels configurable from 2 kHz to 3.5 GHz. Each transmitter channel produces a nominal 1V output and has the most agile frequency, phase and amplitude control of any system on the market. An array of additional options are available including multiple RF transmitters, linear high-power RF amplifiers, digital receiver arrays, low noise figure preamplifiers, a gradient control system, shim unit, MAS spin-speed controller, variable temperature unit, digital lock system and probe/coil interface. With its numerous options, the Apollo can be configured for any NMR, NQR or MRI application."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400249",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.tecmag.com/apollo.htm>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument/NMR console"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "APOLLO console"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000599.
cdao:OBI_0000484 cdao:IAO_0000111 "NMR sample holder"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An NMR sample holder is the part of an NMR instrument, which carries the NMR probe,sample tube and the nmr sample."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400212";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "NMR sample holder"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000968.
cdao:OBI_0000485 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromatography instrument"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Any instrument that is used to carry out a chromatography experiment."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01262",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "chromatography device, defined class?"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chromatography instrument"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000372 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000932.
cdao:OBI_0000486 cdao:IAO_0000111 "continuous wave NMR instrument"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Continuous wave NMR spectrometers are similar to optical spectrometers, but the sample is held in a strong magnetic field, where the frequency of the source is slowly scanned (in some instruments, the source frequency is held constant, and the field is scanned)."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB:<http://teaching.shu.ac.uk/hwb/chemistry/tutorials/molspec/nmr3.htm>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400283";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "continuous wave NMR instrument"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000566.
cdao:OBI_0000487 cdao:IAO_0000111 "fourier transformation NMR instrument"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "In fourier transformation NMR, all frequencies in a spectrum are irradiated simultaneously with a radio frequency pulse. Following the pulse, the nuclei return to thermal equilibrium. A time domain emission signal is recorded by the instrument as the nuclei relax. A frequency domain spectrum is obtained by Fourier transformation."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400284",
                                  "GROUP:<http://teaching.shu.ac.uk/hwb/chemistry/tutorials/molspec/nmr3.htm>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "fourier transformation NMR instrument"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000566.
cdao:OBI_0000489 cdao:IAO_0000111 "nitrogen phosphorous detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The nitrogen phosphorus detector (NPD) (sometimes called the thermionic detector) is a very sensitive, specific detector the design of which, is based on the FID. Physically the sensor appears to be very similar to the FID but, in fact, operates on an entirely different principle. The nitrogen phosphorous detector (sometimes called the thermionic detector) is a very sensitive but specific detector that responds almost exclusively to nitrogen and phosphorous compounds. It is based on the flame ionization detector but differs in that it contains a rubidium or cesium silicate (glass) bead situated in a heater coil, a little distance from the hydrogen flame. If the detector is to respond to both nitrogen and phosphorous then the hydrogen flow should be minimal so that the gas does not ignite at the jet. If the detector is to respond to phosphorous only, a large flow of hydrogen is used which is burnt at the jet. The heated bead emits electrons by thermionic emission. These electrons are collected under a potential of a few volts by an appropriately placed anode, and provides a background current. When a solute containing nitrogen or phosphorous is eluted from the column, the partially combusted nitrogen and phosphorous materials are adsorbed on the surface of the bead. The adsorbed material reduces the work function of the surface and, as consequence, the emission of electrons is increased which raises the current collected at the electrode. The sensitivity of the detector to phosphorous is about 10-12 gram per ml and for nitrogen about 10-11 gram per ml at a signal to nose ratio of 2. The alkali bead as a finite life and needs regular replacement."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01089",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/topics/nitrogen/phosphorus/detector.html>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "nitrogen phosphorous detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000637.
cdao:OBI_0000490 cdao:IAO_0000111 "cation exchange column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A cation exchange column is a chromatography column that is used in cation exchange chromatography."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01096",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "cation exchange column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000560.
cdao:OBI_0000491 cdao:IAO_0000111 "direct detection NMR probe"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An NMR probe designed to allow the direct detection of acquisition nuclei."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400280";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "direct detection NMR probe"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000516.
cdao:OBI_0000492 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker B-ACS system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The Bruker Automatic Sample Changer (B-ACS 60/120), used in conjunction with Bruker DISNMR, UXNMR or XWIN-NMR software, provides dialog-guided facilities which allow the user to easily and effectively perform automatic (continuous) experiments. Features include a 60 or 120 sample capacity, random accessing of samples, positive sample identification with the optional bar code reader, and temperature control of individual samples with the optional sample heater unit."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400210",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/automation.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker B-ACS system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000464.
cdao:OBI_0000493 cdao:IAO_0000111 "rapid resolution column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A rapid resolution column is a chromatography column as marketed by Agilent, which is used with a rapid resolution cartridge to ensure a fast chromatography process with good separation resolution."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01102",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "rapid resolution column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000932,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000372 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000494 cdao:IAO_0000111 "liquid chromatography autosampler"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Designed to perform capillary LC with injection of sample volumes ranging from nL to L."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01061",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "liquid chromatography autosampler"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000485.
cdao:OBI_0000495 cdao:IAO_0000111 "vacuum degasser"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A degassing system used for degassing solvents in liquid chromatography. Dissolved gasses, usually nitrogen and oxygen from the air, tend to be evolved in the mobile phase as the pressure is reduced when the mobile phase leaves the liquid chromatography column and enters the detector. Gasses in the mobile phase in the detector can produce completely unacceptable noise and, thus, must be removed. The dissolved gasses were originally removed under vacuum but, unfortunately, are soon replaced if the solvent is left in contact with air at atmospheric pressure. For this reason degassing is now usually carried out by bubbling helium through the mobile phase reservoirs. Secondly, vacuum is used in the thermionic detector. This consists of a device, very similar in design to the thermionic valve which is attached to a vacuum and a small quantity of the eluent from a gas chromatography column allowed to bleed through it. Helium is used as the carrier gas. The presence of solute vapor causes the thermionic current to fall. This type of detector tends to become contaminated rather readily."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01053",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/topics/vacuum.html>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "vacuum degasser"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000589.
cdao:OBI_0000496 cdao:IAO_0000111 "capillary column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A capillary column is a thin tube with a small inner diameter, usually around 0.5 mm."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01066",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "capillary column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000497 cdao:IAO_0000111 "sample inlet"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The column inlet (or injector) provides the means to introduce a sample into a continuous flow of carrier gas. The inlet is a piece of hardware attached to the column head."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB:<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_chromatography#Inlets>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01044";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "sample inlet"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000048.
cdao:OBI_0000498 cdao:IAO_0000111 "NMR tube washing system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An automatic cleaning system for NMR tubes that removes previous probe and sample residues in order to allow for tube recycling."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400204",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "NMR tube washing system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000968.
cdao:OBI_0000499 cdao:IAO_0000111 "NMR console"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A component of an NMR instrument that controls the activities of the other components."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400015";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument, TODO: same as or part of acquisition computer?"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "NMR console"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000968.
cdao:OBI_0000500 cdao:IAO_0000111 "dual loop autosampler"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A dual loop autosampler is an autosampler that is designed for handling both analytical (10 mL/min flow rate) to preparative scale sample purification (100 mL/min flow rate)."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01063",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chem.agilent.com/scripts/pds.asp?lpage=17149>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "dual loop autosampler"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000494.
cdao:OBI_0000501 cdao:IAO_0000111 "variable wavelength detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A chromatography detector, that can detect signals within a certain range at user-defined wavelengths."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01079",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "variable wavelength detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000832.
cdao:OBI_0000503 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker LC-NMR platform"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The LC-NMR/MS setup was first introduced by Bruker BioSpin in 1999. An LC-NMR system including a Bruker Peak Sampling Unit (BPSU-36) was coupled with a Bruker Daltonics esquire series ion trap mass spectrometer via a Bruker NMR-MS interface (BNMI). Since October 2004 the Bruker Daltonics microTOF-LC time-of-flight mass spectrometer can also be integrated in an LC-NMR setup."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400276",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/hyphenation_lcnmr_ms.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "hyphenated NMR instrument platform",
                                  "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker LC-NMR platform"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000596.
cdao:OBI_0000504 cdao:IAO_0000111 "sample injection system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An automated chromatography system that injects the sample into the chromatography columns in order to increase speed and minimize human involvement in the purification process for  better reproducibility."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01057";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "sample injection system"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000048.
cdao:OBI_0000505 cdao:IAO_0000111 "multiple wavelength detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A chromatography detector, that can detect many discrete wavelengths in parallel and produces a multiple wavelength chromatographic profile."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01078";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "multiple wavelength detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000832.
cdao:OBI_0000506 cdao:IAO_0000111 "photoionization detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The selective determination of aromatic hydrocarbons or organo-heteroatom species is the job of the photoionization detector (PID). This device uses ultraviolet light as a means of ionizing an analyte exiting from a GC column. The ions produced by this process are collected by electrodes. The current generated is therefore a measure of the analyte concentration. f the amount of ionization is reproducible for a given compound, pressure, and light source then the current collected at the PID's reaction cell electrodes is reproducibly proportional to the amount of that compound entering the cell. The reason why the compounds that are routinely analyzed are either aromatic hydrocarbons or heteroatom containing compounds (like organosulfur or organophosphorus species) is because these species have ionization potentials (IP) that are within reach of commercially available UV lamps. The available lamp energies range from 8.3 to 11.7 ev, that is, lambda max ranging from 150 nm to 106 nm. Although most PIDs have only one lamp, lamps in the PID are exchanged depending on the compound selectivity required in the analysis."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "PID"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01090",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chemistry.adelaide.edu.au/external/soc-rel/content/pid.htm>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "photoionization detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000637.
cdao:OBI_0000507 cdao:IAO_0000111 "gas generator"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An instrument that generates gases for use with the gas chromatograph. Previously gas was obtained from gas tanks or gas cylinders. However, over the past decade the use of gas generators have become more popular as it avoids having gases at high pressure in the laboratory which is perceived by some as potentially dangerous. In addition, the use of a hydrogen generator avoids the use of a cylinder of hydrogen at high pressure which is also perceived by some as a serious fire hazard despite the fact that they have been used in laboratories, quite safely for nearly a century."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01033",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/GC/Gas-Supplies/Pure-Air-Generators./rs5.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "gas chromatography equipment"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "gas generator"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000542.
cdao:OBI_0000508 cdao:IAO_0000111 "column jacket"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A column jacket is a piece of column chromatography equipment that covers a column in order to ensure thermoisolation and create a controllable thermostatic microenvironment."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01276",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "column jacket"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000048.
cdao:OBI_0000509 cdao:IAO_0000111 "electron capture detector"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The electron capture detector is a GC detector that uses a radioactive Beta emitter (electrons) to ionize some of the carrier gas and produce a current between a biased pair of electrodes. When organic molecules that contain electronegative functional groups, such as halogens, phosphorous, and nitro groups pass by the detector, they capture some of the electrons and reduce the current measured between the electrodes."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "ECD"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB:<http://homepages.onsnet.nu/%7Ealkema/html/whatisgc.html>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01085";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "electron capture detector"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000637.
cdao:OBI_0000510 cdao:IAO_0000111 "reversed phase column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A reversed phase column is a chromatography column in which the mobile phase is more polar than the stationary phase. Its counterpart is the normal phase column."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01106",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "reversed phase column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000511 cdao:IAO_0000111 "injector lubricant"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A lubricant used in liquid chromatography that eases sample injector penetration."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01118",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "injector lubricant"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000601.
cdao:OBI_0000512 cdao:IAO_0000111 "isolation of cell population";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "removing CD4+ cells from PBMCs using magnetic beads.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a process in which a population of cells with certain characteristics is isolated from a larger population";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person: Bjoern Peters";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "isolation of cell population";
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100060 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0600014,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100060 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000681 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000513 cdao:IAO_0000111 "DISCOVERY console"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The Discovery console is a Windows XP Professional-based, integrated console designed especially for Solid-State NMR. The console includes everything needed to interface to any magnet and solids probe - from computer to cables to duplexing network."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400247";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument/NMR console"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "DISCOVERY console"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000599.
cdao:OBI_0000514 cdao:IAO_0000111 "Bruker AMX series NMR instrument"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A series of older Bruker NMR magnets, now out of production. The Bruker AMX500 has proven an extremely reliable workhorse, with excellent lineshape yielding superior water suppression even without gradients. The Oxford 11.7 Tesla 5.2 cm bore magnet rests on a TMC vibration damping table. Homogeneity is controlled by a BSN-18 and BSN-2 with 19 shim controls. In addition to the 5 mm triple resonance probe, the AMX is equipped with a 10mm broadband observe probe."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400240",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.tufts.edu/med/biochemistry/NMR/amx500.html>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "Bruker AMX series NMR instrument"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000596.
cdao:OBI_0000515 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromatofocusing column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A chromatofocusing column is a chromatography column in which a resin is equilibrated at one pH and eluted at a second pH. The use of a weak ion-exchange resin causes a pH gradient to be formed at the solvent front owing to the buffering action of the resin. This pH gradient in turn leads to an ordering of proteins by isoelectric point. Molecules of charge sign opposite the resin bind; those of charge sign like the resin do not bind."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01209",
                                  "WEB:<http://www.bioprocessintl.com/default.asp?page=glossary&TopicID=1>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chromatofocusing column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000516 cdao:IAO_0000111 "NMR probe"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Part of an NMR instrument that detects the signals emitted from a sample. No single probe can perform the full range of experiments, and probes that are designed to perform more than one type of measurement usually suffer from performance compromises. The probe represents a rather fragile single point of failure that can render an NMR system completely unusable if the probe is dropped or otherwise damaged. Probes are usually characterised by Sample diameter and Frequency.\\n  alt The instrument that transmits and receives radiofrequency to and from the NMR sample."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400014",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "NMR probe"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000566 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000050 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000453 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000085 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000832.
cdao:OBI_0000517 cdao:IAO_0000111 "NMR magnet"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A magnet which induces a certain frequency (MHz) and which has a certain bore diameter.\\n  alt The NMR signal is a natural physical property of the certain atomic nuclei but it can only be detected with an external magnetic field. A magnet is a fundamental part of an NMR instrument which induces an electromagnetic force field (RF pulse) and by this excites and aligns the spins of the electrons of the NMR acquisition nucleus. It is usually a big (superconducting) electromagnet which is cooled by liquid helium and can be adjusted to a frequency between 200 and 950 MHz. The magnetic field strength is measured in Tesla or Gauss."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400185";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "NMR magnet"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000968.
cdao:OBI_0000518 cdao:IAO_0000111 "trap column"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A trap column is a chromatography column which is used prior to a, e.g. mass spectrometry, separation to clean up or concentrate controlled amounts of samples prior to elution to a detector."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01261",
                                  "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "trap column"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000038.
cdao:OBI_0000519 cdao:IAO_0000111 "flow probe"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An NMR probe that allows the automatized flow-through of a sample. The sample is aspirated via a syringe pump into the Flow probe, the NMR spectrum is acquired and when the experiment is complete, the sample is returned to back to an external source (well plate) or flushed to waste. Sometimes pulsed field gradients (PFG) can be established in flow probes."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB:<http://www.varianinc.com/cgi-bin/nav?products/NMR/accessory/auto_samplers/vast/index&cid=HFIH>"@en,
                                  "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400131";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "NMR device"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "flow probe"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000516.
cdao:OBI_0000520 cdao:IAO_0000111 "clinical chemistry assay";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Influence of hydroxyethyl starch (6% HES 130/0.4) administration on hematology and clinical chemistry parameters.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An analyte assay which uses analytical methods to produce measurements and data on the concentration of chemical parameters (analytes) present in a bodily fluid collected from an organism.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "detection of analyte in blood sample",
                                  "chemical pathology";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "url:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinical_chemistry";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "clinical chemistry assay";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000443,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> ([<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:OBI_0000275
