                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0001051 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:IAO_0000109
                                                                                                                                  cdao:OBI_0001573) ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>] ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000749 cdao:IAO_0000111 "CART"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A CART (classification and regression trees) is a data transformation method for producing a classification or regression model with a tree-based structure."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "James Malone"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "classification and regression trees";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "BOOK: David J. Hand, Heikki Mannila and Padhraic Smyth (2001) Principles of Data Mining."@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "CART"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000707,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000704 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000750 cdao:IAO_0000111 "independent variable specification";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "In a study in which gene expression is measured in patients between 8 month to 4 years old that have mild or severe malaria and in which the hypothesis is that gene expression in that age group is a function of disease status, disease status is the independent variable.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a directive information entity that is part of a study design. Independent variables are entities whose values are selected to determine its relationship to an observed phenomenon (the dependent variable). In such an experiment, an attempt is made to find evidence that the values of the independent variable determine the values of the dependent variable (that which is being measured). The independent variable can be changed as required, and its values do not represent a problem requiring explanation in an analysis, but are taken simply as given. The dependent variable on the other hand, usually cannot be directly controlled"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2/2/2009 Original definition - In the design of experiments, independent variables are those whose values are controlled or selected by the person experimenting (experimenter) to determine its relationship to an observed phenomenon (the dependent variable). In such an experiment, an attempt is made to find evidence that the values of the independent variable determine the values of the dependent variable (that which is being measured). The independent variable can be changed as required, and its values do not represent a problem requiring explanation in an analysis, but are taken simply as given. The dependent variable on the other hand, usually cannot be directly controlled."@en,
                                  """In the Philly 2013 workshop the label was chosen to distinguish it from \"dependent variable\" as used in statistical modelling. See: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistical_modeling""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters",
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "experimental factor",
                                  "independent variable";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "Web: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dependent_and_independent_variables";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "2009-03-16: work has been done on this term during during the OBI workshop winter 2009 and the current definition was considered acceptable for use in OBI. If there is a need to modify thisdefinition please notify OBI.";
                 cdao:OBI_0001847 "study factor";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "study design independent variable"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:IAO_0000033,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0500000 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000050 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0000751 cdao:IAO_0000111 "dependent variable specification";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "In a study in which gene expression is measured in patients between 8 month to 4 years old that have mild or severe malaria and in which the hypothesis is that gene expression in that age group is a function of disease status, the gene expression is the dependent variable. ";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "dependent variable specification is part of a study design. The dependent variable is the event studied and expected to change when the independent variable varies."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2/2/2009 In the design of experiments, independent variables are those whose values are controlled or selected by the person experimenting (experimenter) to determine its relationship to an observed phenomenon (the dependent variable). In such an experiment, an attempt is made to find evidence that the values of the independent variable determine the values of the dependent variable (that which is being measured). The independent variable can be changed as required, and its values do not represent a problem requiring explanation in an analysis, but are taken simply as given. The dependent variable on the other hand, usually cannot be directly controlled."@en,
                                  """In the Philly 2013 workshop the label was chosen to distinguish it from \"dependent variable\" as used in statistical modelling. See: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistical_modeling""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert",
                                  "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "dependent variable";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dependent_and_independent_variables";
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "2009-03-16: work has been done on this term during during the OBI workshop winter 2009 and the current definition was considered acceptable for use in OBI. If there is a need to modify thisdefinition please notify OBI.";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "study design dependent variable"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0500000 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000050 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:IAO_0000033.
