                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0001146 cdao:IAO_0000111 "binding assay";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Determination of KD value for an antibody binding a protein using a BIACORE assay. Using plate bound antigen in an ELISA to determine if a mixture of serum antibodies bind the antigen. The following are NOT binding assays, as the desired output is not binding data: RNA microarray experiments to determine levels of gene expression. ChIP experiments to determine where in DNA a transcription factor binds. Using an IL-2 antibody on an ELISA plate to determine presence of IL-2 after stimulating a T cell culture.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "An assay with the objective to characterize the disposition of two or more material entities to form a complex.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Bjoern Peters",
                                  "Randi Vita",
                                  "Jason Greenbaum";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "binding assay";
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0001181 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0001588 ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:IAO_0000136 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>] ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000070.
cdao:OBI_0001147 cdao:IAO_0000111 "cell culture expansion"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a processual entity that results in the increase of cell numbers"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "including grow of yeast and bacteria"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert, Jie Zheng"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "MO_758 grow"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 """BP:
add it as subclass of 'cell culturing'
JZ:
No 'cell culturing' in OBI
Has term 'cell co-culturing' and  'maintaining cell culture'. Don't think either of it fit. So leave the term under process."""@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "cell culture expansion"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000094,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000456 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> ([<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100060 ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]
                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100060 ; 
                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000299 ; 
                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0001148 cdao:IAO_0000111 "gene knock out"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a genetic transformation that renders a gene non-functional, e.g. due to a point mutation, or the removal of all, or part of, the gene using recombinant methods."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert, Jie Zheng"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "MO_771 gene_knock_out"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "gene knock out"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0600043.
cdao:OBI_0001149 cdao:IAO_0000111 "gene knock in"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """a genetic transformation that involves the insertion of a protein coding cDNA sequence at a particular locus in an organism's chromosome. Typically, this is done in mice since the technology for this process is more refined, and because mouse embryonic stem cells are easily manipulated. The difference between knock-in technology and transgenic technology is that a knock-in involves a gene inserted into a specific locus, and is a \"targeted\" insertion."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert, Jie Zheng";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene_Knock-in"@en,
                                  "MO_437 gene_knock_in"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "gene knock in"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0600043.
cdao:OBI_0001150 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chromosomal substitution"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A genetic transformation in which all, or part, of a chromosome from a donor replaces that of the recipient. It does not include chromosome recombination. For single gene insertion, use the term 'gene knock in'. "@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert, Jie Zheng"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "MO_995 chromosomal_substitution"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chromosomal substitution"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0600043.
cdao:OBI_0001151 cdao:IAO_0000111 "genetically modified material"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a material entity, organism or cell,  that is the output of a genetic transformation process. "@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jie Zheng"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "term is proposed by BP on Oct 25, 2010 dev call"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "genetically modified material"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000047;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> (cdao:OBI_0302859
                                                                                                           [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:CL_0000000
                                                                                                                                                           [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0600043 ; 
