cdao:OBI_0100039 cdao:IAO_0000111 "fragment derived from protein"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "the peptide with sequence SIINFEKL, which is eluted from a cell expressing hen egg lysozyme"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A material entity which is derived from a  protein"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 """original term: protein fragment split into synthetic polypeptide and fragment derived from protein
THE DEFINITION OF THIS SUGGESTS WE COVER THIS ALREADY IN PEPTIDE/POLYPETIDE. DO WE NEED THIS AND CAN WE DEAL WITH IT IN SOME OTHER WAY?  JAMES"""@en,
                                  "BP:03/21/2010:obsoleted as the class is no longer necessary, and we would otherwise need all kinds of 'fragment derived from' classes. Instead, use composite terms with the relationship 'derived from' some protein OR derived from some part_of protein.",
                                  "PRS:22022008. result from protocol_application where input=protein and output=polypeptide or peptide (to capture: derives_from protein)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: IEDB"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
