                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0200196 cdao:IAO_0000111 "correlation study objective";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A data transformation objective in which correlation is obtained (often measured as a correlation coefficient, ρ) which indicates the strength and direction of a relationship between two random variables.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "correlation study objective";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0200166.
cdao:OBI_0200197 cdao:IAO_0000111 "spectrum analysis objective";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "Calculation of characteristic path length in mass spectrometry";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is a data transformation objective where the aim is to analyse some aspect of spectral data by some data transformation process. ";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                                  "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "spectrum analysis objective";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0200166.
cdao:OBI_0200198 cdao:IAO_0000111 "tandem mass spectrometry";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "A precursor ion is selected in the first stage, allowed to fragment and then all resultant masses are scanned in the second mass analyzer and detected in the detector that is positioned after the second mass analyzer. This experiment is commonly performed to identify transitions used for quantification by tandem MS.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Tandem mass spectrometry is a data transformation that uses two or more analyzers separated by a region in which ions can be induced to fragment by transfer of energy (frequently by collision with other molecules).";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                                  "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "tandem mass spectrometry";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0200085,
                                 [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0200197 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
cdao:OBI_0200199 cdao:IAO_0000111 "gas chromatography mass spectrometry";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 """Gas chromatography mass spectrometry is a data transformation combining mass spectrometry and  
gas chromatography for the qualitative as well as quantitative  
determinations of compounds.""";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                                  "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "gas chromatography mass spectrometry";
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0200197 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0200085.
cdao:OBI_0200200 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chi square test";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "The chi-square test is a data transformation with the objective of statistical hypothesis testing, in which the sampling distribution of the test statistic is a chi-square distribution when the null hypothesis is true, or any in which this is asymptotically true, meaning that the sampling distribution (if the null hypothesis is true) can be made to approximate a chi-square distribution as closely as desired by making the sample size large enough.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard",
                                  "PERSON: James Malone";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "chi square test";
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000675 ; 
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000417 ; 
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>],
                                 cdao:OBI_0000673.
cdao:OBI_0200201 cdao:IAO_0000111 "ANOVA";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "ANOVA or analysis of variance is a data transformation in which a statistical test of whether the means of several groups are all equal.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "James Malone";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "ANOVA";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0200000.
cdao:OBI_0300310 cdao:IAO_0000111 "sequential design"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 17710740.Pharm Stat. 2007 Aug 20.Sequential design approaches for bioequivalence studies with crossover designs."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "Any design in which the decision as to whether to enroll the next patient, pair of patients, or block of patients is determined by whether the cumulative treatment difference for all previous patients is within specified limits.  Enrollment is continued if the difference does not exceed the limits.  It is terminated if it does"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "MUSC"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "Provenance: OCI"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "sequential design"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000115.
cdao:OBI_0300311 cdao:IAO_0000111 "observation design"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 12387964.Lancet. 2002 Oct 12;360(9340):1144-9.Deficiency of antibacterial peptides in patients with morbus Kostmann: an observation study."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "observation design is a study design in which subjects are monitored in the absence of any active intervention by experimentalists."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "observation design"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0500000.
cdao:OBI_0302714 cdao:IAO_0000111 "collection (of entities of organismal origin)"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18037794. Magn Reson Med Sci. 2007;6(3):139-46. Imaging of a large collection of human embryo using a super-parallel MR microscope.[the Orsay Museum has a nice collection of Impressionnist paintings]"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a collection is a bfo:aggregate object, that is a set of material object of the same kind"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2009-11-04, MC: Entity of organismal origin has been deprecated a while ago. We still have collection (of entities of organismal origin). I am not sure we could replace with collection of material entity without altering the meaning (i.e. deprecating the class). In addition, if we do deprecate that class, should we just assert the children under material entity?",
                                  "03/17/2010: obsoleted (on call), and replaced by 'material entity' and/or specimen. No need for the 'collection' part of this class any more after merging bfo:aggregate object into material entity, and by dealing with 'specimen' rather than with entities of organismal origin.",
                                  "added during 22-02-2008 biomaterial call to distinguish library and population"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Susanna Sansone";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "set, group, ensemble"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000103;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "PRS: How can we distinguish with 'collection' as the process of collecting entities, (eg. data collection, urine collection)"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_collection (of entities of organismal origin)"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0302716 cdao:IAO_0000111 "pool of specimens"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A pool of specimens is a mixture of a population of samples which have been gathered from one or more sample populations, obtained by the physical process of mixing individual specimens, e.g.  mixing the DNA collected from the individual fish."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "check with advisors as to how to represent multiple instances of any class? a set of specimens which have been gathered from one or more sample_populations, obtained by the physical process of mixing individual specimens, e.g.  mixing the DNA collected from the individual fish"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: CEBS";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "pool of specimens"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:OBI_0000953;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:OBI_0100051
                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> (cdao:OBI_0000652
                                                                                                                                                                                                                  [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0100051 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000293 ; 
                                                                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>] ; 
                                                                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:OBI_0000312 ; 
                                                                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>]) ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>].
cdao:OBI_0302729 cdao:IAO_0000111 "chemical solution"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18289311.Anesth Analg. 2008 Apr;106(4):1078-86.Less impairment of hemostasis and reduced blood loss in pigs after resuscitation from hemorrhagic shock using the small-volume concept with hypertonic saline/hydroxyethyl starch as compared to administration of 4% gelatin or 6% hydroxyethyl starch solution."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "A material entity  that is made up of at least 2 scattered molecular aggregates, one playing the role of solvent and the other one playing the role of solute."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                                  "PERSON: Bjoern Peters";
                 cdao:IAO_0000118 "liquid chemical solution"@en;
