cdao:OBI_0302743 cdao:IAO_0000111 "liver"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 """PMID: 2104732. Caudate lobe of the liver: anatomy, embryology, and pathology.
AJR Am J Roentgenol. 1990 Jan;154(1):87-93."""@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "liver is an anatomical entity which constituent are mainly hepatocytes, which has a function of detoxification, hematopoietic center, glucose and fat metabolism management. liver is only found in animals , all Vertebrates and some families of invertebrates"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial Branch";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "PRS: Test. added for evaluation and validation of possible imports from CARO (or other anatomical resources)"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_liver"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
cdao:OBI_0302745 cdao:IAO_0000111 "adipose tissue"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "PMID: 18435934.Fatty acid composition of adipose tissue and blood in humans and its use as a biomarker of dietary intake.Prog Lipid Res. 2008 Apr 4."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000125;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "adipose tissue is a tissue which main constituents are adipocytes. adipose tissue can be classified base on its location (site) but also based on adipocyte subtypes (brown or white) which reflect functional differences and is only found in animals, Vertebrates or invertebrates."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial derived";
                 cdao:IAO_0000231 cdao:IAO_0000228;
                 cdao:IAO_0000232 "PRS: this class has been added during major biomaterial.owl cleanup for evaluation and testing of imports from CARO"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "obsolete_adipose tissue"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ObsoleteClass>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> true.
