cdao:OBI_1110061 cdao:IAO_0000111 "exposure resulting in immune reactivity";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000120;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a process in which an organism (host) is exposed to some material entity, which results in an immune reactivity";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "IEDB"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "IEDB"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "exposure resulting in immune reactivity"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:GO_0008150.
cdao:OBI_1110082 cdao:IAO_0000111 "immunogen role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "any entity capable of eliciting an immune response when introduced to components of the immune system"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "IEDB"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "IEDB"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "immunogen role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000023.
cdao:OBI_1110083 cdao:IAO_0000111 "host of immune response role";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000123;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "is a role borne by an organism. It is realized by the organism during an immunization or an immune response taking place inside or on the surface of the organism, and in which the responding or stimulated immune system is part of the host."@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "03/21/2010: This sense of 'host' is used not only in infectious diseases but also allergy, cancer, transplantation, etc. which is why it is needed separately from the 'host of infectious agent' meaning, which will be imported from IDO.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000117 "IEDB"@en;
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "IEDB"@en;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "host of immune response role"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> (cdao:GO_0006955
