cdao:OBI_1110108 cdao:IAO_0000111 "material to be added";
                 cdao:IAO_0000112 "A mixture of peptides that is being added into a cell culture.";
                 cdao:IAO_0000114 cdao:IAO_0000122;
                 cdao:IAO_0000115 "a material that is added to another one in a material combination process";
                 cdao:IAO_0000116 "2010/02/24  Alan Ruttenberg: I think this might generate confusion as the common use of the term would consider something to be a specimen during the realization of the role, not only if it bears it. However having this class as a probe, or for display, or as a macro might be useful. Ideally we would mark or segregate such classes",
                                  "10/26/09: This defined class is used as a 'macro expression' to reduce the  size of the IEDB export";
                 cdao:IAO_0000119 "IEDB";
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                 rdfs:label "material to be added";
                 rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000040;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OBI_0000319 ; 
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:RO_0000087 ; 
                                                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
