cdao:OGMS_0000023 cdao:IAO_0000111 "phenotype";
                  cdao:IAO_0000115 "A (combination of) quality(ies) of an organism determined by the interaction of its genetic make-up and environment that differentiates specific instances of a species from other instances of the same species."@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:ogms.owl;
                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                  rdfs:label "phenotype";
                  rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000019.
cdao:OGMS_0000031 cdao:IAO_0000111 "disease";
                  cdao:IAO_0000115 "A disposition (i) to undergo pathological processes that (ii) exists in an organism because of one or more disorders in that organism."@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:ogms.owl;
                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                  rdfs:label "disease";
                  rdfs:subClassOf cdao:BFO_0000016.
cdao:OGMS_0000063 cdao:IAO_0000111 "disease course";
                  cdao:IAO_0000115 "The totality of all processes through which a given disease instance is realized."@en;
                  cdao:IAO_0000232 """replace 'OBI:occurrence of disease', need to add logical definition
The axioms of OBI occurence of disease:
Equivalent classes:
realizes some disease
Superclasses:
'has part' some 'pathologic process'
'has participant' some 
    (organism
     and ('has role' some 'host of immune response role'))
biological_process
realizes some 'host of immune response role'""";
                  cdao:IAO_0000412 cdao:ogms.owl;
                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                  rdfs:label "disease course";
                  rdfs:subClassOf cdao:GO_0008150;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> cdao:OGMS_0000031 ; 
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> cdao:BFO_0000055 ; 
                                                                   a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>].
