cdao:RO_0000052 cdao:IAO_0000111 "inheres in"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000112 "this red color inheres in this apple"@en,
                                 "this fragility inheres in this vase"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a specifically dependent continuant (the dependent) and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the dependent specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A dependent inheres in its bearer at all times for which the dependent exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "inheres_in"@en;
                cdao:RO_0001900 cdao:RO_0001901;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:label "inheres in"@en;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000053];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000053.
cdao:RO_0000053 cdao:IAO_0000111 "bearer of"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000112 "this apple is bearer of this red color"@en,
                                 "this vase is bearer of this fragility"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a specifically dependent continuant (the dependent), in which the dependent specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A bearer can have many dependents, and its dependents can exist for different periods of time, but none of its dependents can exist when the bearer does not exist."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "is bearer of"@en,
                                 "bearer_of"@en;
                cdao:RO_0001900 cdao:RO_0001901;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:label "bearer of"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000020;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000052].
cdao:RO_0000056 cdao:IAO_0000111 "participates in"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000112 "this blood clot participates in this blood coagulation"@en,
                                 "this input material (or this output material) participates in this process"@en,
                                 "this investigator participates in this investigation"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a continuant and a process, in which the continuant is somehow involved in the process"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "participates_in"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000002;
                rdfs:label "participates in"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000003;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000057];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000057.
cdao:RO_0000057 cdao:IAO_0000111 "has participant"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000112 "this process has participant this input material (or this output material)"@en,
                                 "this investigation has participant this investigator"@en,
                                 "this blood coagulation has participant this blood clot"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a process and a continuant, in which the continuant is somehow involved in the process"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "Has_participant is a primitive instance-level relation between a process, a continuant, and a time at which the continuant participates in some way in the process. The relation obtains, for example, when this particular process of oxygen exchange across this particular alveolar membrane has_participant this particular sample of hemoglobin at this particular time."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "has_participant"@en;
                <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:has_participant";
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000003;
                rdfs:label "has participant"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000002;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000056].
cdao:RO_0000058 cdao:IAO_0000112 "An investigator reads a protocol and forms a plan to carry out an assay. The plan is a realizable entity (a specifically dependent continuant) that concretizes the protocol (a generically dependent continuant), and both depend on the investigator (an independent continuant). The plan is then realized by the assay (a process)."@en,
                                 "A journal article is an information artifact that inheres in some number of printed journals. For each copy of the printed journal there is some quality that carries the journal article, such as a pattern of ink. The journal article (a generically dependent continuant) is concretized as the quality (a specifically dependent continuant), and both depend on that copy of the printed journal (an independent continuant)."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "A relationship between a generically dependent continuant and a specifically dependent continuant, in which the generically dependent continuant depends on some independent continuant in virtue of the fact that the specifically dependent continuant also depends on that same independent continuant. A generically dependent continuant may be concretized as multiple specifically dependent continuants."@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000031;
                rdfs:label "is concretized as"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000020;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000059];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000059.
cdao:RO_0000059 cdao:IAO_0000112 "An investigator reads a protocol and forms a plan to carry out an assay. The plan is a realizable entity (a specifically dependent continuant) that concretizes the protocol (a generically dependent continuant), and both depend on the investigator (an independent continuant). The plan is then realized by the assay (a process)."@en,
                                 "A journal article is an information artifact that inheres in some number of printed journals. For each copy of the printed journal there is some quality that carries the journal article, such as a pattern of ink. The quality (a specifically dependent continuant) concretizes the journal article (a generically dependent continuant), and both depend on that copy of the printed journal (an independent continuant)."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "A relationship between a specifically dependent continuant and a generically dependent continuant, in which the generically dependent continuant depends on some independent continuant in virtue of the fact that the specifically dependent continuant also depends on that same independent continuant. Multiple specifically dependent continuants can concretize the same generically dependent continuant."@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000020;
                rdfs:label "concretizes"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000031;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000058].
cdao:RO_0000079 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this catalysis function is a function of this enzyme"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a function and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the function specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A function inheres in its bearer at all times for which the function exists, however the function need not be realized at all the times that the function exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "is function of"@en,
                                 "function_of"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000034;
                rdfs:label "function of"@en;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000052;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000085];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000085.
cdao:RO_0000080 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this red color is a quality of this apple"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a quality and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A quality inheres in its bearer at all times for which the quality exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "is quality of"@en,
                                 "quality_of"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:label "quality of"@en;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000052;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000086];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000086.
cdao:RO_0000081 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this investigator role is a role of this person"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between a role and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A role inheres in its bearer at all times for which the role exists, however the role need not be realized at all the times that the role exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "role_of"@en,
                                 "is role of"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:label "role of"@en;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000052;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000087];
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000087.
cdao:RO_0000085 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this enzyme has function this catalysis function (more colloquially: this enzyme has this catalysis function)"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a function, in which the function specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A bearer can have many functions, and its functions can exist for different periods of time, but none of its functions can exist when the bearer does not exist. A function need not be realized at all the times that the function exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "has_function"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000004;
                rdfs:label "has function"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000034;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000053;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000079].
cdao:RO_0000086 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this apple has quality this red color"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a quality, in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A bearer can have many qualities, and its qualities can exist for different periods of time, but none of its qualities can exist when the bearer does not exist."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "has_quality"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:label "has quality"@en;
                rdfs:range cdao:BFO_0000019;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf cdao:RO_0000053;
                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> [<http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> cdao:RO_0000080].
cdao:RO_0000087 cdao:IAO_0000112 "this person has role this investigator role (more colloquially: this person has this role of investigator)"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000115 "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a role, in which the role specifically depends on the bearer for its existence"@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000116 "A bearer can have many roles, and its roles can exist for different periods of time, but none of its roles can exist when the bearer does not exist. A role need not be realized at all the times that the role exists."@en;
                cdao:IAO_0000118 "has_role"@en;
                a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                rdfs:domain cdao:BFO_0000004;
